        <ns0:rule id="b06440ab-bec9-58f7-ae54-0f60b095522d" name="HH3 Port Source Rules - pp. 27-27" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 27
SONS OF HORUS CHIEFTAINS – HQ CHOICE - – 125 POINTS
                             WS       BS        S         T        W         I         A        LD

Chieftain                    5         4        4         4         1        4         2         9

Standard Bearer              5         4        4         4         2        4         2         9

UNIT TYPE                                                 UNIT COMPOSITION

Standard Bearer – Infantry (Character)                             4 Chieftains

Chieftain – Infantry                                               1 Standard Bearer

WARGEAR                                                            SPECIAL RULES

    •    Banestrike Bolter (Chieftains only)                       Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
    •    Legion Standard (Standard Bearer only)                    Chieftain Retinue
    •    Bolt Pistol                                               Chosen Warriors
    •    Chainsword                                                Kingslayers
    •    Frag and Krak Grenades
    •    Power armor
    •    Boarding Shield

A Chieftain squad may include

    •    Up to 5 additional Chieftains – 20 points each

Any model max exchange its chainsword with one of the following options

    •    Chainaxe – 2 points
    •    Power Weapon – 10 points
    •    Power Fist – 15 points

The entire unit may exchange its power armor for Artificer armor for 5 points per model

Chieftain Retinue

A Chieftain Squad in a Detachment that includes at least one model with the Master of the Legion special rule may be
selected as a Retinue Squad instead of as an HQ choice. The model with the Master of the Legion special rule is referred
to as the Retinue Squad’s Leader for the purposes of this special rule (if the Detachment includes more than one model
with both the Master of the Legion special rule then the controlling player selects one as the unit’s Leader). A Chieftain
Squad selected as a Retinue Squad does not use up a Force Organisation slot and is considered part of the same unit as
the model selected as its Leader. A Chieftain Squad selected as a Retinue Squad must be deployed with the model
selected as its Leader deployed as part of the unit and the Leader may not voluntarily leave the Retinue Squad during
play.

Kingslayers

When any models with this special rule are used to make Melee Attacks against an enemy unit that includes any models
with the Independent Character special rule, all failed To Hit rolls of ‘1’ may be re-rolled. When a model with this special
rule that is Engaged in a Challenge is used to make Melee Attacks against a model with the Independent Character
special rule, all failed To Hit rolls may be re-rolled.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="125.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
