      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="db4c8032-ae77-526d-90ce-d07e2586b1ce" name="HH3 Port Source Rules - pp. 29-29" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 29
SPACE WOLVES JORLUND HUNTER PACK – TROOPS CHOICE– 125 POINTS
                                WS       BS         S         T           W       I         A       LD

Hunter                          4         4         4         4           1       4         1       8

Hunt Master                     4         4         4         4           1       4         2       9

UNIT TYPE                                                     UNIT COMPOSITION

Hunt Master – Infantry (Character)                            1 Hunt Master

Hunters – Infantry                                            4 Hunters

WARGEAR                                                                   SPECIAL RULES

     •    Chainsword                                          Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)
     •    Hand Flamer                                         Crusader
     •    Frag and Krak Grenades                              Scouring Tempest
     •    Power armor                                         Scout
                                                              Support Squad

DEDICATED TRANSPORT

A Space Wolves Jorlund Hunter Pack numbering no more than 10 models may purchase a Legion Rhino Transport, Legion
Termite Assault Drill or Land Raider Phobos or Proteus as a dedicated transport.

OPTIONS

The Space Wolves Jorlund Hunter pack l may include up to 10 additional Hunters for 15 points Each

For every 5 models in the squad, one model may exchange their hand flamer for

     -    Flamer – 5 points
     -    Volkite Serpenta – 5 points

One model in the squad may take a Vexilla for 10 points

The Hunt Master may take :

     -    Melta bombs – 5 points
     -    Artificer armor – 5 points

The Hunt Master may replace his hand flamer with a plasma pistol for 10 points

The Hunt master may replace his Chainsword with a Frost Blade for 15 points

Scouring Tempest

Once per battle, during the Shooting phase of one of their turns as the Active player, the controlling player of a unit made
up entirely of models with this special rule may choose to activate Scouring Tempest before the unit is selected to make a
Shooting Attack. Until the end of the Phase, all Flame weapons in the unit gain the Pinning and Torrent (3") special rule</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="125.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
