      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="b4c57e18-4a83-5855-a33b-29451ff6354b" name="HH3 Port Source Rules - pp. 32-33" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 32
IRON HANDS MORLOCK TERMINATOR SQUADS- HQ CHOICE - 150 POINTS
                              WS        BS       S      T         W         I            A   LD

Morlock                       5         4        4      4         2         4            2   8

Procurant                     5         4        4      4         2         4            3   9



UNIT TYPE                                               UNIT COMPOSITION

Augmentor – Infantry (Character)                                  1 Augmentor

Morlocks – Infantry                                               2 Morlocks

WARGEAR                                                           SPECIAL RULES

     •    Combi-bolter                                  Legiones Astartes (Iron Hands)
     •    Power Weapon                                  Stubborn
     •    Legion Cataphractii Terminator armor          Loyalist
                                                        Avernian Retinue
                                                        Fate of the Gorgon


DEDICATED TRANSPORT

An Iron Hands Morlock Terminator squad may purchase a land raider Proteus or Phobos as a dedicated transport

Options

The Iron Hands Morlock Terminator squad may take up to 2 additional Morlocks for 35 points each

One Morlock may exchange their combi-bolter for a legion standard for 20 points

One Morlock may take an augury scanner for 10 points

One Morlock may take a Nuncio Vox for 10 points

Any model in the unit may exchange their power weapon for one of the following

     •    Power Fist – 10 points
     •    Lightning Claw – 10 points
     •    Chainfist – 15 points

Any model in the unit may exchange their combi-bolter for one of the following

     •    Volkite Charger – free
     •    Graviton gun – 10 points

The Augementor may exchange their combi-bolter for a volkite culverin for 10 points

PAGE 33
Special Rules
Avernian Retinue

An Iron Hands Morlock Terminator squad in a Detachment that includes at least one model with the Master of
the Legion special rule may be selected as a Retinue Squad instead of as an HQ choice. The model with the
Master of the Legion special rule is referred to as the Retinue Squad’s Leader for the purposes of this special
rule (if the Detachment includes more than one model with both the Master of the Legion special rule then
the controlling player selects one as the unit’s Leader). An Iron Hands Morlock Terminator squad selected as
a Retinue Squad does not use up a Force Organisation slot and is considered part of the same unit as the
model selected as its Leader. An Iron Hands Morlock Terminator squad selected as a Retinue Squad must be
deployed with the model selected as its Leader deployed as part of the unit and the Leader may not
voluntarily leave the Retinue Squad during play.

Fate of the Gorgon

If selected as part of a Detachment in an army that includes Ferrus Manus, an Iron Hands Morlock Terminator
Squad gains the Chosen Warriors special rule. If selected as part of a Detachment in an army that does not
include Ferrus Manus, an Iron Hands Morlock Terminator Squad gains the Preferred Enemy (Emperor’s
Children) special rule</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
