      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="549f576d-9dc4-5f93-ac58-55d3fb59b14a" name="HH3 Port Source Rules - pp. 51-52" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 51
LEGION SATURNINE TERMINATOR SQUAD- ELITES CHOICE - 200 POINTS
                            WS        BS       S         T        W         I        A         LD

Saturnine Terminator        4         4        4         5         2        3        2             8

Saturnine Sergeant          4         4        4         5         2        3        2             9



UNIT TYPE                                                UNIT COMPOSITION

Saturnine Sergeant – Infantry (Character)                1 Saturnine Sergeant

Saturnine Terminator – Infantry                          2 Saturnine Terminator

WARGEAR                                                           SPECIAL RULES

    •     Plasma Bombard                                          Legiones Astartes
    •     Saturnine disruption fist
    •     Legion Saturnine Terminator armor
    •     Thermal diffraction grid
    •     Occulix Targeting auspex




DEDICATED TRANSPORT

An Iron Hands Saturnine Terminator squad may purchase a legion land raider Proteus or Phobos as a dedicated transport
if it numbers no more than 3 models. A Unit of more than 3 models may purchase a Legion Spartan Assault tank as a
dedicated transport.

Options

Any model in the unit may have its Saturnine disruption fist exchanged for one of the following:

    -     Plasma Bombard – Free
    -     Twin Linked Heavy Disintegrator – 10 points.

Any model in the unit may have its plasma bombard exchanged for one twin linked heavy disintegrator for 10 points.

Any model in the unit may have with a Saturnine disruption fist may have one particle shredder selected for is for 15
points per model.

PAGE 52
Occulix Targeting Auspex

When a model with this special rule is selected to make a shooting attack, if that model remained stationary
in the movement phase, it may fire two weapons this shooting phase. Both attacks must be made at the same
target.



Thermal diffraction grid

If a unit is made of entirely of models equipped with a Thermal Diffraction Field reduces the strength of all
attacks inflicted by a Flame. Mclta, Plasma or Volkite weapon by 1, to a minimum of 1. In addition the models
are granted a 4+ Feel No Pain roll against any wound: inflicted by the Gets hot special rule, in the case of the
Saturine Dreadnought, it may roll a 4+ to ignore a wound suffered from Gets Hot! In the same way.

Saturnine Terminator Armor

Provides a 2+ armor save and a 4+ invulnerable save. The wearer gains +1 Toughness but reduces initiative by
1 (Already included in profile). Grants the Slow and Purposeful special rule and Very Bulky special rules. In
addition, Models in Saturnine Terminator Armor may reroll armor saves against any template weapons. If a
model in this armor is ever reduced to 0 wounds, roll a D6, on a 6 it Explodes!



Saturnine Weapons

Plasma Bombard

        RANGE        S            AP       TYPE

        24’         7             2        Heavy 1, Small Blast, Gets hot, Barrage.

Particle Shredder

        RANGE        S            AP       TYPE

        Template     5            3        Assault 1, Rending, Gets hot



Saturnine Disruption Fist

        RANGE        S            AP       TYPE

        Melee       +2            2        Melee, Unwieldy, Specialist Weapon. Disruptor

        Disruptor: Any model that suffers an unsaved wound from a weapon with this rule takes 2 wounds
        instead.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="200.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
