      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="9b7f8018-63a2-51dc-bb69-b87e7d9cfed4" name="HH3 Port Source Rules - pp. 75-75" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 75
Hors Ascended Uses all of the rules for regular Horus from the Legions book from 1.0. His stat line changes to the following and gains a
number of additional rules such as gains Rage, Feel no Pain (4+), A Dark Fate, The Power of Chaos Eternal and The Spreading
Corruption. In addition, Horus Ascended counts as having the Endless Hatred special rule.




   Horus Ascended............................................1000 Points – LORD OF WAR CHOICE
          WS         BS        S          T          W         I          A         LD

           8         6         8          8          8         6          6          10

A Dark Fate

The first time in any battle that Horus Ascended loses his last Wound, or is otherwise removed from play as a casualty, the
model is instead placed into Reserves with a single Wound remaining – any unit Horus Ascended was part of remains in
play, even a Retinue or other unit that would normally not allow the removal of a model from the unit. After having been
placed in Reserves due to this special rule, Horus Ascended may choose to re-enter play, with the controlling player
making Reserves rolls for the model as per the normal rules. If the Slay the Warlord objective, or any other objective that
requires the enemy Warlord be removed as a casualty to score Victory points, is in effect then it is still triggered when
Horus Ascended is moved into Reserves due to this special rule – and may be triggered a second time if Horus Ascended
returns to play and is removed as a casualty again.



The Power of Chaos Eternal

Once per battle, at the start of any Assault phase (whether Horus Ascended’ s controlling player is the Active or Reactive
player), Horus Ascended’ s controlling player may choose to activate the Power of Chaos Eternal. Once activated, Horus
Ascended increases his Strength and Toughness Characteristics to 10 for the duration of the Assault phase and ignores
all the effects of the Unwieldy special rule on attacks made with Worldbreaker. Once the Assault phase is ended, all
combats being fought have been resolved and the effects of the Power of Chaos Eternal have ended, Horus Ascended
automatically suffers Perils of the Warp – but any Wounds caused must be allocated to friendly models in the same unit
as Horus Ascended, if any such models exist, before they are allocated to Horus Ascended.

The Spreading Corruption:

A unit composed entirely of models with the Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus) special fails a Morale check it does not
Fall Back as per the standard rules, but instead suffers D3 automatic Wounds with no saves or Damage Mitigation rolls of
any kind allowed. These wounds are randomly allocated.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="1000.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="1cc6c984-40f1-5fd1-92b0-66d560fbc2dc" name="Dark Mechanicum Proscribed Techno Arcana" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="58b1125e-2d7d-5563-9510-843f4e946481" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="761aa8c3-ae1c-50d3-9bd4-dd42d135425d" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="2e345ac5-a6d6-52e8-a350-02e1fa638a6a" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 3-6" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 3
THE ORDERS OF THE PROSCRIBED TECHNO ARCANA

Any Traitor aligned Magos Prime/Archmagos Prime can take one of the following Techno Arcana instead of the usual ones.
This does not mean they cannot take the usual ones. All of the same rules for using Techno Arcana still apply.
Cybertheurgic Weapons function in the same way as Cybertheurgy powers but are mainly shooting attacks on enemy
units. A model may still only use one Cybertheurgy power per turn.




MALEFIKITE ………………………………………………………………………+30 Points
A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains all of the special rules listed here:

• Bonds of Corruption: Any unit with a Cybernetica Cortex that is in the same Detachment as a model with this
Proscribed Techno-arcana may have the Ruinous Cybernetica special rule.

 • Magister Malefica: A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains the Machina Malefica Cybertheurgy powers, but
the controlling player may not select any other Cybertheurgy powers from those available for the model.

• Malignant Vector: During any Shooting phase, instead of making a Shooting Attack, the controlling player of a model
with this Proscribed Techno-arcana may select any friendly unit with the Cybernetica Cortex Special rule has at least one
model within 2" of model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana and roll a D6 for it on the following table:

D6 RESULT

1 The selected model suffers no further effect.

2-3 All models count as passing their Leadership test for their Ruinous Cybernetica Roll for the turn.

4+ All models count as passing their Leadership test for their Ruinous Cybernetica Roll for the rest of the game.



RUINOUS CYBERNETICA

At the start of the controlling player’s Shooting phase, that player can make a Leadership test for any units made up
entirely of models with this special rule. If that test is passed, until the end of the turn:

• All models in the unit are not subject to the Programmed Behaviour special rule.

• At the start of the Charge sub-phase, a Charge must be declared for this unit if there is an enemy unit within 12", and the
closest enemy unit must always be selected as the target of this Charge if possible (if multiple eligible units are equally
distant then the controlling player must select one of those eligible units to be the target of the Charge). This means that
in some cases they may charge a different target then they shot in the shooting phase.

If that test is failed, the unit suffers one Wound, allocated by the controlling player. No Saving Throws or Damage
Mitigation rolls of any kind may be made against this Wound.

PAGE 4
CYBERTHEURGY POWERS: MACHINA MALEFICA

A Cybertheurgist with this Arcana gains all of the Rites, Weapons and other special rules listed here.



Indicium Malefica (Cybertheurgic Power)

A Cybertheurgist with this Cybertheurgic Rite may use it instead of making a Shooting Attack in the controlling player’s
Shooting phase. The model makes a Cybertheurgy test with no modifiers. If they fail, noting happens. If a double 6 is
rolled, the model takes a wound with no saves of any kind allowed. If Successful, the controlling player may select a
single enemy unit and roll a D6 for each model (excluding Vehicles) in that unit that is within 6" of the Cybertheurgist
model. For each result that equals or beats that model’s Save characteristic, that model’s unit suffers one Wound,
allocated by the Active player. Saving Throws and Damage Mitigation rolls can be taken against this Wound as normal. The
controlling player then rolls a D6 for each affected Vehicle. For each result of 6, one affected model with the Vehicle Unit
Type suffers a Crew Stunned result from the Vehicle Damage table and loses a hull point.

The Cybertheurgist may choose to add a -2 modifier to the Cybertheurgy test. If successful, every enemy model within 6"
of the Cybertheurgist model is affected instead.



Diabolis Quiritatus (Cybertheurgic Weapon)

Range    S         AP       TYPE

18’      6         3        Assault 3, Data-djinn, Rending, Cybertheurgic Focus

Data-Djinn: This attack only works on Vehicles and models with the Cybernetica Cortex Special rule.

Cybertheurgic Focus: Before making any To Hit rolls with this weapon, the Cybertheurgist must make a Cybertheurgy
test with no modifiers. If the Check is passed then the Cybertheurgist may attack as normal using the profile shown for
this weapon. If the Check is failed then the Cybertheurgist suffers Cybertheurgic Feedback, and nothing happens. On a
double 6, the model suffers a wound with no saves of any kind allowed and cannot use the weapon this turn.

PAGE 5
NEKROTEK (ARCHMAGOS PRIME ONLY)..……………………………..+30 points
A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains all of the special rules listed here:

• Mekanika Exanimate: Any unit composed entirely of models with the Cybernetica Cortex Special rule in the same
Detachment as a model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains the It Will Not Die special rule.

• Magos Necroteknica: A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains the Ephemera Nekrotek Cybertheurgy Arcana
(see below), but may not select any other Cybertheurgy powers from those available to it.

• Nekromorphic Locus: Increase the Wounds Characteristic of a model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana by 1.

CYBERTHEURGIC ARCANA: EPHEMERA NEKROTEK

A Cybertheurgist with this Arcana gains all of the listed Rites, Weapons and other special rules.

Viteum Adficio (Cybertheurgy Power)

A Cybertheurgist with this Cybertheurgic Rite may use it at the end of the controlling player’s Movement phase. The
controlling player rolls for a Cybertheurgy test with no modifiers. On a roll of a double 6 the user takes a wound with no
saves of any kind allowed. If Successful, the controlling player may select one friendly unit from the Mechanicum Faction
that is within 6" of the Cybertheurgist and roll up to three D6. For each result of 4+, one model in that unit suffers 1 Wound
(or loses 1 Hull Point if it is a Vehicle unit), and the Cybertheurgist regains 1 lost Wound. Saving Throws and Damage
Mitigation rolls cannot be taken against these Wounds.

The Cybertheurgist may choose to add a -2 modifier to the Cybertheurgy test before using this Cybertheurgic Rite. If
successful, the controlling player can re-roll any of the three D6 when using this Cybertheurgic Rite.

Tactus Mors (Cybertheurgic Weapon)

The model may attempt to use the following as a close combat weapon instead of another weapon.

``Range            S         AP       TYPE

    -           As user      4        Melee, Unwieldy, Haywire, Cybertheurgic Focus



 Cybertheurgic Focus: Before making any To Hit rolls with this weapon, the Cybertheurgist must make a Cybertheurgy
test with no modifiers. If the Check is passed then the Cybertheurgist may attack as normal using the profile shown for
this weapon. If the Check is failed then the Cybertheurgist suffers Cybertheurgic Feedback, and nothing happens. On a
double 6, the model suffers a wound with no saves of any kind allowed and cannot use the weapon this turn.

PAGE 6
MALAMINA ……………………………………………………………………….+35 points
A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains all of the special rules listed here:

• Magos Abominatio: For each model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana in a Detachment, the controlling player can
grant one Infernus Abomination in the same Detachment the Preferred Enemy (Loyalists) Special rule.

• Armatus Malevolus: Any model in the same Detachment as a model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana can replace a
power weapon or automata power blades for abomination blades for free.

Abomination Blades

Range    S         AP       TYPE

    -    User      2        Melee, Specialist Weapon, Rampage, Bloodthirsty



Bloodthirsty: Add +1 to To Hit rolls made for this weapon if any models in the target unit have been removed as casualties
already and it is below its starting strength or if there are models have not been removed as a casualty that are below their
starting Wounds Characteristic.




ÆTHERTEK ……………………………………………………………………….+25 points
A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains all of the special rules listed here:

 • Mechanika Ætherika: For each model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana in a Detachment, the controlling player can
include one Decimator unit in the same Detachment as a non-compulsory Troops choice.

• Opus Malefica: A model with this Proscribed Techno-arcana gains the Anima Malefica Cybertheurgic Arcana (See the
Daemon Engines section), but may not select any other Cybertheurgic Arcana from those available to it.

• Magos Invocatus: While a unit composed entirely of models that are Daemon Engines and within 6" of a model with this
Proscribed Techno-arcana, are not affected by special rules that negatively modify their Characteristics (other than
Wounds or Hull Points) such as Blind or concussive and ignore the effects of Crew shaken and Crew Stunned.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="8e213e23-683d-5b2c-954f-8c5e841b3529" name="Krios Irradiation Engine" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="58b1125e-2d7d-5563-9510-843f4e946481" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="cf1139b3-6dbe-55bf-a6f9-de87f61e631b" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="800988a4-21a8-546d-be06-c7e752f7c863" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 7-7" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 7
Mechanicum Krios Irradiation engine
A Mechanicum Krios may exchange its Lightning cannon with an Irradiation Blaster for 40 points

Irradiation Blaster

An Irradiation Blaster has two profiles, one must be picked when firing and if part of a unit of Krios, they must all choose
the same one.

                                       Range              S         AP        TYPE

                      Focused          16’                7         3         Heavy 1, Fleshbane, Rad-Phage,

                                                                              Radiation Beam

                      Dispersed        Hellstorm          2         5         Heavy 1, Fleshbane, Rad-Phage,



Radiation Beam

When the weapon is fired, draw a 1" wide line from the end of the gun barrel up to the listed range of the weapon. The
initial target for the weapon (the first model in the beam ’ s path) must be an enemy model.

    -    All models (friend and enemy) caught in the beam area (excepting the ring tank) su er a hit with the listed pro le
         of the weapon, except Zooming Flyers, Swooping Monstrous Creatures, and Flying Gargantuan Creatures that
         cannot be affected or targeted.
    -    Units struck receive a number of hits equal to the number of their models caught in the path of the beam;
         casualties are removed from affected units using the normal rules for removing casualties.
    -    If the beam strikes a Super-heavy vehicle, Gargantuan Creature or large intact building/fortification (bastion
         sized or larger), the attack is blocked and its line of effect will go no further. The blocking target will, however,
         super 1+D3 separate hits, rather than just 1.
    -     If a vehicle transporting models suffers a penetrating hit from the Irradiation Blaster, the occupants inside suffer
         D6 Str 2 AP- Fleshbane hits, in addition to any other effects. Casualties are assigned by the controlling player.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="c43ce8c5-b8dd-5759-8b41-f5696cb822af" name="Corrupted Engines and Malefic Cybertheurgy" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="58b1125e-2d7d-5563-9510-843f4e946481" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="acbe424f-daef-5702-bb57-c2b68aef1d49" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="c0c6cacb-ead7-5a38-8932-d67b7b5d2722" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 8-13" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 8
CORRUPTED ENGINES SUPPLEMENTARY LIST



The following section presents rules for using a selection of Corrupted Engines in games of
Warhammer: The Horus Heresy – Age of Darkness 1.0. These rules are Expanded units for
the Mechanicum Army List and may be selected for a Detachment with the Mechanicum
Faction that has the Traitor allegiance, or included as part of an Allied Detachment of that
Faction. The following special rules apply to some or all of the units included in this section
– see the respective profiles for more details, In addition, ignore any Deep strike special
rules for Daemon engines.

Legion Praevian and Corrupted Engines

An army that includes a Legion Praevian may take a single unit of Corrupted Engines
instead of Castellax Battle-automata Maniple or a Vorax Battle-automata Maniple. If a
Corrupted Engine Unit type is chosen via this rule, it does not form part of the same Force
Organisation choice as the Legion Praevian with the Master of Cybernetica special rule and
must instead occupy its own appropriate Force Organisation choice*.

 An army can include a maximum of one unit of Corrupted Engines chosen in this manner,
regardless of the number of Legion Praevians within the army. Additional Legion Praevians
beyond the first may select a Castellax Battle-automata Maniple or a Vorax Battle-
automata Maniple via the Master of Cybernetica rule as normal.

*The chosen unit fills the available slot as if it was selected as a separate choice i.e., a
Decimator chosen via this rule would use a Elites slot when chosen. If none are available, it
cannot be chosen.

PAGE 9
MALEFIC CYBERTHEURGY

The following is an additional Cybertheurgy powers available to any Traitor alligned Mechanicum
armies: A Cybertheurgist that is not Unique, and is part of a Detachment with the Traitor allegiance,
may select the following Anima Malefica Cybertheurgy INSTEAD of other Cybertheurgy powers
available to it. Doing so gives access to each Malefic Cybertheurgy Power.

Cybertheurgic Arcana: Anima Malefica A Cybertheurgist with this Arcana gains all the listed Rites,
Weapon and other special rules.

Animatus Malevolence (Cybertheurgic Rite)

Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Cybertheurgist with this Cybertheurgic Rite may select a
single friendly unit within 12" that is entirely composed of models that are Corrupted Engines and
roll to activate a cyberthurgy power as normal with no modifiers If the test is successful then apply
one of the following effects:

      •   The chosen unit may immediately move a number of inches up to its unmodified Initiative
          Characteristic directly towards the nearest enemy unit. If the chosen unit has mixed
          Initiative Characteristics, use the highest unmodified Characteristic.
      •   All models in the chosen unit improve their Invulnerable Save by 1, to a maximum of 3+,
          until the beginning of the controlling player’s next turn, (e.g., a model with an Invulnerable
          Save of 5+ improves their save to 4+). •
      •   All models in the unit add 1 to their WS and I characteristics until the end of the subsequent
          Assault phase.

The Cybertheurgist’s controlling player may attempt to select two effects instead. If the player
wishes they must roll for the Cybertheurgy power as normal. If the Check is successful then two
different options chosen from the above list may be applied to the target unit instead of one. If the
Check is failed then no options may be chosen – the Corrupted unit then rolls on the Cyberthurgic
Mishap table and apply the effects to all models in the unit

Amthea Excrusis (Cybertheurgic Attack)

Range            Str     AP      Type

18"              5       3       Assault 3, Blind, Deflagrate, Cybertheurgic Focus

Cybertheurgic Focus: Before making any To Hit rolls with this weapon, the Cybertheurgist must
make a Cybertheurgy check as if they were using a cyberthurgy power with no modifiers. If the
Check is passed then the Cybertheurgist may attack as normal using the profile shown for this
weapon. If the Check is failed then the power does nothing, on a double 6 the user takes a wound
with no saving throws allowed.

PAGE 10
KYTAN DAEMON ENGINE OF KHORNE — 525 POINTS
WS 5; BS 3; S 10; Front 13; Side 13; Rear 11; I 5; A 4; HP 6.
Unit Composition: 1 Kytan Daemon Engine. Unit Type: Vehicle (Super-heavy Walker).
Wargear: Kytan gatling cannon; Great Cleaver of Khorne.
Special Rules: Daemon; Daemonforge; Fleet; Crusader; It Will Not Die; Rage; Unstoppable Slaughter; Super-heavy Walker rules (Fear, Hammer of Wrath, Invincible Behemoth, Move Through Cover, Relentless, Smash and Strikedown).
Unstoppable Slaughter: If the Kytan destroys a target in its Shooting phase with its attacks, it may charge a different target in the Assault phase.
Kytan gatling cannon: Range 48"; S 8; AP 3; Heavy 8, Pinning.
Great Cleaver of Khorne: Range -; S D; AP 1; Melee.
Selection note from source: may be used as a Lords of War choice in Chaos Space Marines, Khorne Daemonkin or Chaos Daemons; in Khorne Daemonkin it has Blood for the Blood God; it may be selected instead of a Khorne Lord of Skulls where that war machine is available.

PAGE 11
BLOOD SLAUGHTERERS OF KHORNE — 130 POINTS PER MODEL
WS 5; BS 1; S 6; Front 13; Side 12; Rear 10; I 4; A 3; HP 3.
Unit Composition: 1–3 Blood Slaughterers. Unit Type: Vehicle (Walker).
Wargear: Two Dreadnought close combat weapons.
Special Rules: Daemon of Khorne; Daemonic Resilience; Deep Strike; Fleet; Fury of Khorne; Rampage; Blind Fury.
Option: Any Blood Slaughterer may replace one Dreadnought close combat weapon with an impaler +5 points.
Impaler: Range 12"; S 8; AP 3; Assault 1, Impaler.
Fury of Khorne: on a successful charge, gains +D3 Attacks instead of the usual +1; loses Rampage bonus when charging.
Blind Fury: in Movement it must move as far as possible towards the closest visible enemy and must consolidate toward the closest visible enemy; in Shooting, if able it must Run or otherwise move toward the closest visible enemy; if a viable enemy is in charge range it must charge the closest viable enemy.
Impaler: after a successful hit, on a 4+ drag a vehicle hit by a successful penetrating hit, or a Monstrous Creature wounded by the attack, towards the Blood Slaughterer until it is within charge range; if this brings it within 2", the Blood Slaughterer counts as having charged it. Infantry may be repositioned as described by the source. Buildings, Super-heavy Vehicles and Gargantuan Creatures cannot be dragged.

PAGE 12
CHAOS DECIMATOR — 205 POINTS
WS 3; BS 3; S 8; Front 13; Side 12; Rear 11; I 3; A 4; HP 3.
Unit Composition: 1 Decimator Daemon Engine. Unit Type: Vehicle (Walker).
Wargear: Two Decimator siege claws with in-built heavy flamers.
Special Rules shown: Daemon; Unholy Vigour; Deep Strike; Daemonic Resilience.
Options: either siege claw/heavy flamer may be replaced (each replacement reduces Attacks by 1): Butcher cannon +20; Storm laser +15; Soulburner petard +10. A single siege claw/heavy flamer may instead be replaced with a heavy conversion beamer +35. May also take searchlight +1 and smoke launchers +3.
Decimator relic weapons: Siege claws — S User, AP2, Melee, Shred, Smash; Butcher cannon — 36", S8 AP4 Heavy 4; Storm laser — 36", S6 AP3 Heavy D3+2; Soulburner petard — 24", S5 AP5 Ordnance 1, Large Blast (5"), Rending. Heavy conversion beamer — up to 18": S6 AP- Heavy 1, Large Blast (5"), Firing Calibration; 18–42": S8 AP4 Heavy 1, Large Blast (5"), Firing Calibration; 42–72": S10 AP1 Heavy 1, Large Blast (5"), Firing Calibration.
Unholy Vigour: Weapon Destroyed or Immobilised results may be ignored on a 5+. If Wrecked (but not Explodes), leave a marker; at the start of subsequent controlling turns roll D6 before models move: on 6 it returns near its position as if by Deep Strike with weapons/mobility restored and D3 Hull Points; on 3–5 remain marker; on 1–2 it is permanently Wrecked.
Daemonic Resilience: ignores Crew Shaken and Crew Stunned on a 2+.
Smash note: a building/transport suffering a penetrating hit from a Decimator Smash attack causes units inside to suffer D6 heavy-flamer hits for each heavy flamer the Decimator has, in addition to other damage.
Firing Calibration: heavy conversion beamer cannot fire if the carrying model moved in the same turn, regardless of Relentless or vehicle status.

PAGE 13
GREATER BRASS SCORPION OF KHORNE — 700 POINTS
WS 3; BS 3; S 10; Front 14; Side 13; Rear 10; I 3; A 6; HP 9.
Unit Composition: 1 Greater Brass Scorpion. Unit Type: Super-heavy Walker.
Wargear: one Scorpion cannon; one Soulburner cannon; two Hellmaw cannons.
Special Rules: Daemon; Frenzied Charge; Runes of the Blood God; Doomsday Reactor; It Will Not Die; Multi-legged Terror.
Frenzied Charge: roll 3D6 and add the result for charge distance.
Runes of the Blood God: a Psyker targeting the Greater Brass Scorpion with a psychic power automatically suffers Perils of the Warp after the power, whether or not it passed.
Doomsday Reactor: +2 modifier on Catastrophic Damage table.
Scorpion cannon: 36", S6 AP3, Heavy 10. Soulburner cannon: 24", S10 AP2, Primary Weapon 1, Large Blast (5"), Ignores Cover Saves. Hellmaw cannon: Template, S6 AP3, Assault 1.
Multi-legged Terror: when making a Stomp attack, makes D3+2 Stomps.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="3693f276-646c-5181-a0ee-193ab3fb4820" name="Questoris Household Dark Blessings" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="e22f91fc-2eff-5193-b02a-1bb1921864f0" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="0487bce8-5911-5204-9f9c-feece61c9b21" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="f43a93d4-3601-5c28-9e1e-85231915b1ec" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 14-17" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 14
QUESTORIS HOUSEHOLD DARK BLESSINGS



The following section presents expanded options for Questoris Household list.

Any Lords of War choice selected as part of a Questoris Household Detachment may
select one upgrade from those included in these rules, but note that some upgrades are
limited to certain units or may only be selected a limited number of times as noted in their
description.

A Lords of War choice selected from the Divisio Tactica: Questoris Household army list to
fill a Lords of War Detachment slot selected for an army whose Primary Detachment is not
a Questoris Knight Household Detachment may select a single option from those included
here.

A model with the Loyalist special rule cannot have any of the upgrades included within the
following section.

Any model that has one or more upgrades from the following section gains the Traitor
special rule if they did not already have it.

If a model within a Detachment has any upgrades included in the following section, no
model within the same army can have a Household Ranks upgrade.

So an Army either has to pick Household ranks or Dark Blessings and can’t have both in the
same army. Each type of Dark Blessing is applicable to any choice on the force organization
chart.

PAGE 15
DARK BLESSINGS:

                          CONQUEROR OF WORLDS – 80 POINTS

A model with this upgrade gains the Character special rule and increases its Weapon Skill
and Ballistic Skill Characteristics by +1. In addition, if the Questoris Household
Detachment is the Primary Detachment of the army, then a model with this upgrade must
be chosen as the army’s Warlord. An Acastus Knight Porphyrion or Acastus Knight Asterius
may not be given this Dark Blessing. If selected as the army’s Warlord, a model with this
upgrade automatically gains the following Warlord Trait:

Master of the Household – Any friendly model with the Vehicle Type and super heavy
walkers within 8" of a Warlord with this Warlord Trait may fire overwatch, ignoring the usual
restriction for Super Heavy Walkers and vehicles.

                               HEEDLESS SLAUGHTER - FREE

A model with this Dark Blessing gains the Character special rule and must reduce its
Weapon Skill and Ballistic Skill Characteristics by -1. In addition, for each model with this
Dark Blessing, all models in a single unit made up entirely of models that are Armigers,
selected as part of the same Detachment, gain the Rage special rule for no additional
points cost.

                               Malevolent Artifice +50 points

At the end of each of the controlling player’s turns in which a model with this upgrade
inflicts at least one unsaved Wound or Hull Point with a weapon with the Melee type, it
gains the It Will Not Die (6+) special rule until the end of the battle. If the model already has
the It Will Not Die (X) special rule, it increases the value of X by 1, up to a maximum of 4+.



                                Encroaching Ruin +40 points

A model with this upgrade increases its Ballistic Skill Characteristic by +1 and gains the
Character Special Rule and Commanding Presence special rule.

Commanding Presence: Armiger units that have at least one model within 6" of one or
more friendly models with this special rule at the start of a turn increase their Movement
Characteristic by +2 until the end of that player turn.

PAGE 16
Putrid Corruption +45 points
A model with this upgrade must reduce its Movement Characteristic by -2 and gains the Unrelenting special
rule. An Acastus Knight Porphyrion or Acastus Knight Asterius may not be given this Dark Blessing.

Unrelenting: Each time a model with this special rule suffers an Explodes result on the Vehicle Damage
chart, it loses 1 extra Hull Point instead of D3, in addition to the Hull Point it loses for the Penetrating Hit.




                                        Infernal Tempest +25 points
A model with this upgrade gains the Character and Psychic Pilot Mastery Level 1 special rules, and the
Infernal Rites Psychic Discipline. When making a Psychic check, a model with this upgrade always counts as
having a Leadership Characteristic of 7 regardless of any modifiers or effects.

Psychic Discipline: Infernal Rites

A Psyker with this Discipline gains the listed Power, weapon and special rules.

Infernal Warding (Psychic Power) - Blessing - Warp Charge 2

The model with this power gains +1 to their Invulnerable Save, to a maximum of 3+, until the start of the
controlling player’s next player turn.

Empyreal Tempest – Witchfire - Warp Charge 2



``Range           S        AP       TYPE

    12’           5        2        Heavy 1, Blast, Guided Fire

Guided Fire: Attacks with this weapon do not require line of sight, but must still be within range.



                               Ravenous Dissolution. ...............+50 points
A model with this upgrade increases its Weapon Skill Characteristic by +1, and gains the Character and the
Marked for Death special rule.

Marked For Death: At the start of the battle, once both armies have set up all their models, including any
units with the Infiltrator special rule, a single enemy unit may be chosen by a player that controls any models
with this special rule – this unit is considered ‘marked for death’. When any models with this special rule
controlled by that player are used to make an attack of any kind against the enemy unit their controlling player
has ‘marked for death’, all failed To Wound and armor penetration rolls of ‘1’ may be re-rolled.

PAGE 17
Rapturous Sensation. .................+65 points

No enemy unit that has one or more models within 8" of a model with this Dark Blessing
may have models within this area without passing a successful Pinning test. Enemy models
also with this area may not fire Overwatch.




                               Formless Distortion. .................+45 points
A model with this upgrade increases its Weapon Skill Characteristic by +1 and gains the Character Special
rule. In addition, it may exchange a single weapon with the Melee type with the following weapon at no
additional cost:

    Range         S        AP       TYPE

    -             10       2        Melee, Reach, Exoshock

Reach:

The model with this special rule fights at +1 Initiative

Exoshock:

If this weapon successfully scores a penetrating hit on a target, roll a D6. On the roll of a 4+, a second
automatic penetrating hit is inflicted on the same target, against which cover saves may not be taken.




Knights and the Character Special rule

Unless otherwise specified, a Knight with the Character special rule may issue and accept
Challenges – While Engaged in a Challenge, a Knight with the Character special rule may
not leave combat or the Challenge and may not make any Stomp attacks.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
