    <ns0:selectionEntry id="eb19507a-9a8b-5f27-a7e2-0db62cf6eb8c" name="New Consul Types" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="2a01812c-043d-538a-bb3b-55f655c7fb1d" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="1c53b732-a9a3-5544-84b5-268ae30421d7" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 19-23" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 19
NEW CONSUL TYPES

Legion Master of Descent Consul                                                +65 points

Wargear and Special Rules

A Centurion with this consul type gains Artificer armor, a refractor field, jump pack and
Strato-Vox. Cannot be equipped with terminator armor, bike or jet bike. In addition, A
Master of Descent gains the Master of Descent special rule

Strato-Vox

Any reserve rolls for a unit that contains a model with a Strato-Vox are automatically
successful. In addition, while any models with equipped with a Strato-vox are on the
battlefield at the beginning of the turn; any reserves rolls for units that wish to deploy via
the deep strike special rule are considered automatically successful as long as they deploy
via the deep strike special rule.

Master of Descent

If a model with this special rule is in reserves and every model in the unit is either jump
infantry or jet pack infantry and wishes to deploy via deep strike, they may deep strike onto
the table on turn 1. Only one unit from an army may make use of this special rule per turn.

PAGE 20
Legion Overseer                                                                       +25 points

Wargear and Special Rules

A Centurion with this consul type gains the Overseer’s retinue, Master of Auxilia and
Support officer special rules.

A Legion Overseer may exchange their Chainsword for a Power lash or Power maul for 15
points

Power Lash

Range               Str       AP        Type

-                   -1        3         Melee, Shred, Reach
Reach

The model with this special rule fights at +1 Initiative

Overseer’s Retinue:

An army that includes a model with this special rule may take a Tercio of 1-3 Auxilia Lasrifle
Sections or 1-3 Imperialis Militia Infantry Squads with no Provenances, as part of the same Force
Organisation choice as the model with this special rule, as an Overseer’s Retinue. Note that any
unit selected through the use of this special rule may not take any Dedicated Transport or Aegis
defence line options. Any Solar Auxilia Rifles Sections included through the use of the Overseer’s
Retinue gain the Legiones Auxilia (X) special rule that corresponds with the Legiones Astartes (X)
special rule that the Legion Overseer they share a Force Organisation choice with has. Additionally,
all models in a Tercio selected as an Overseer’s Retinue use the Leadership Characteristic of the
model with the Legiones Overseer special rule.



Master of Auxilia:

 A model with this special rule must join a Auxilia LasRifle Section or Imperialis Militia Infantry
Squad, chosen by the controlling player that was selected as an Overseer’s Retinue during
deployment and once joined, may not voluntarily leave the unit during the course of any battle and
may only join units selected through the use of the Overseer’s Retinue special rule. Whilst part of a
unit selected as an Overseer’s Retinue, the Legion Overseer automatically passes Look out Sir!
rolls. Additionally, a model with the Master of Auxilia special rule is considered to have the same
variant of the Legiones Auxilia (X) special rule as the models in the unit that they have joined.

PAGE 21
Legion Specific New Consul types

Sons of Horus Legion Dark Emissary                                               +25 points

Wargear

A Dark Emissary gains a Staff of Dark Authority at no additional points cost. A Dark
Emissary may not select a jump pack, Space marine Bike or Space Marine Jetbike.

Staff of Dark Authority

All models with the Traitor Allegiance within 6" of a model with a Staff of Dark Authority,
including that model, increases their Leadership to 10 when taking a Morale check or
Pinning test.


       S      AP      TYPE

       +1      3      Melee, Murderous Strike, Unwieldy




Special Rules

The Dark Emissary gains the Warmaster’s Eye special rule:

Warmaster’s Eye:

If a Dark Emissary is selected as a Compulsory HQ choice in an Allied Detachment that is
part of an army with the Traitor Allegiance, then all models in the Allied Detachment with
the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule gain the Stubborn special rule.

PAGE 22
Imperial Fists Legion Castellan                                                            +20 points

Wargear

A Legion Centurion with the Castellan upgrade gains Hardened armor at no additional cost.

A Legion Centurion with the Castellan upgrade must select one of the following options: -
Master-crafted heavy bolter ......................................................................................Free
- Master-crafted autocannon..............................................................................+5 points
- Iliastus assault cannon ...................................................................................+10 points

In addition, a Castellan may not select a jump pack, Legion Space marine bike, Legion
Space marine jetbike, combat shield, boarding shield, power fist, Solarite power gauntlet,
lightning claw(s) or any weapon with the Two-handed special rule.

Special Rules

A Castellan gains the Fire Support special rule.

Fire Support:

When making an attack with a Heavy weapon, a Castellan may increase the number of
attacks made with that weapon by +1 when making a Shooting Attack (for example, a
Castellan making a Shooting Attack with a Heavy 3 weapon would roll an additional dice for
its attacks, rolling four dice in total). In addition, any Legion Heavy Support Squads in the
same Detachment as a Castellan gain the Implacable Advance Special rule.

PAGE 23
Emperor’s Children Legion Phoenix Warden                                       +30 points

Wargear

A Legion Centurion with the Phoenix Warden upgrade gains a Phoenix Power Spear and an
Iron Halo at no additional cost.

In addition, a Phoenix Warden MUST be equipped with Tartaros Terminator Armor which is
not included in the cost.

Special Rules

A Legion Centurion with the Phoenix Warden upgrade and a Phoenix Terminator Squad that
he is attached to gain the Skill Unmatched Special rule. In Addition the Phoenix Warden has
the Living Icon Special rule.

Skill Unmatched

When a combat that involves one or models with this special rule is resolved, before the
start of Initiative step 10 the controlling player of any models in that combat with this
special rule may select one of the three following options and apply the effects of that
option to all models with this special rule for the duration of that Assault phase. When a
unit contains more than one model with this special rule, then all models in that unit must
select the same option if one is chosen:

• A Perfect Guard: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, any to hit rolls made by the opponent suffer a -1 to hit to a maximum of 6+, but must
reduce their Attacks Characteristic by -1.

• A Perfect Strike: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, they increase their to hit roll by +1 to a maximum of 3+, but must reduce their
Attacks Characteristic by -1.

• A Perfect Fury: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, they must increase their Attacks by +1, but must reduce their Weapon Skill by -1.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="92d59b56-3584-567e-b782-2c7b67aae0e9" name="Legiones Auxilia" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="c9584246-8101-5f66-ae1c-022faa5103a0" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="3515503c-29cf-5021-8da9-b2f639c4b76e" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="3dab5945-b33d-518b-9654-707d0cac92f8" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 24-26" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 24
THE LEGIONES AUXILIA SPECIAL RULE

The Legiones Auxilia special rule is intended to represent Solar Auxilia cohorts that fight alongside
the forces of the Legiones Astartes during the Horus Heresy, showcasing the unique
specialisations, equipment and tactics they adopted in doing so. The Legiones Auxilia special rule
may only be applied to an Allied Detachment selected using the Solar Auxilia Army List and where
the Primary Detachment’s Warlord has the Legiones Astartes special rule. The Legiones Auxilia
special rule is currently intended to be used alongside a Warlord with a base version of the
Legiones Astartes special rule and may not be applied to an Allied Detachment selected from the
Solar Auxilia Army List in the same army as a Detachment containing models with the Legiones
Hereticus, Legiones Astartes (Shattered Legions) or Legiones Astartes (Blackshields) special rules.

Each variant of the Legiones Auxilia special rule is associated with the matching Legion and can
only be selected alongside a Primary Detachment whose Warlord has this corresponding Legiones
Astartes special rule – e.g., Legiones Auxilia (Dark Angels) and Legiones Astartes (Dark Angels). Any
version of the Legiones Auxilia special rule being applied to an Allied Detachment drawn from the
Solar Auxilia Army List must be selected during army selection and noted on the army roster. An
Allied Detachment drawn from the Solar Auxilia Army List which has had a version of the Legiones
Auxilia special rule applied to it still belongs to the Imperial Army Faction and the Solar Auxilia Sub-
faction. However, it is always considered to have the ‘Fellow Warriors’ level of Alliance with the
Space Marine Faction they correspond with, unless they would already have the ‘Sworn Brothers’
level of Alliance.

Additionally, if a unit which contains one or more models with the Legiones Auxilia special rule has
at least one model within 12" of a friendly unit containing one or more models with the
corresponding Legiones Astartes special rule when that unit fails a Morale check, the unit
containing models with Legiones Auxilia is immediately Pinned.

All models with the Disciplined Fire Special Rule gain the Legiones Auxilia (x) special rule.



The following Legiones Auxilia rules are only the ones that could possibly be used as part of my
local play group

PAGE 25
LEGIONES AUXILIA (EMPEROR’S CHILDREN)

THE ART OF SUFFERING

Whenever a Shooting Attack causes a unit containing one or more models with the Legiones Auxilia
(Emperor’s Children) special rule to have one or more models removed as casualties, all models in the unit
with the Legiones Auxilia (Emperor’s Children) special rule gain the Hammer of Wrath special rule until the
end of their controlling player’s next turn.

                                   LEGIONES AUXILIA (IMPERIAL FISTS)

STEADFAST

A unit entirely composed of models with both the Legiones Auxilia (Imperial Fists) special rule and is a scoring
unit, increases all Cover Saves granted by terrain by one (i.e., from 6+ to 5+). This only increases existing
Cover Saves and does not grant one when in terrain that does not normally grant a Cover Save. This rule
cannot increase a Cover Save to better than 3+.



                                   LEGIONES AUXILIA (IRON WARRIORS)

SHOT-SHROUDED

Models with the Legiones Auxilia (Iron Warriors) special rule do not take morale tests from shooting attacks
and may reroll failed Pinning tests.

                                   LEGIONES AUXILIA (SPACE WOLVES)

THE EARS OF MORKAI

When an enemy unit deploys using Infiltrate, Outflank, or Deep strike, Units with the Legiones Auxilia (Space
Wolves) gain the Ignores Cover Special rule for all shooting attacks on the first turn or the turn they arrive from
reserves. When making overwatch attacks, All models with this special rule gain Ignores Cover.

                                   LEGIONES AUXILIA (IRON HANDS)

CEREBRAL AUGMENTS

When a unit entirely composed of models with the Legiones Auxilia (Iron Hands) special rule fails a Morale
check owing to casualties in the Shooting phase, it does not Fall Back as per the standard rules, but instead
suffers D3 automatic Wounds with no Saves of any kind allowed but Damage Mitigation rolls such as the Feel
No Pain special rule may still be used to negate these Wounds).



                                   LEGIONES AUXILIA (ULTRAMARINES)

COMBINED ARMS

When a unit containing one or more models with the Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines) special rule declares a
Charge against an enemy unit which has had one or more models removed as casualties as a result of a
Shooting Attack made by a model with the Legiones Auxilia (Ultramarines) special rule in the same Game
Turn, that enemy unit may not fire Overwatch against the charging Ultramarines unit.

PAGE 26
LEGIONES AUXILIA (THOUSAND SONS)

PSY-SHOCK

Any friendly model with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule which suffers Perils of the Warp
while within 12" of a unit entirely composed of models with the Legiones Auxilia (Thousand Sons) special may
choose to allocate all of the Wounds inflicted by Perils of the Warp to the unit containing models with the
Legiones Auxilia (Thousand Sons) special rule. Additionally, all models with the Legiones Auxilia (Thousand
Sons) special rule gain the Adamantium Will special rule.

                                  LEGIONES AUXILIA (SONS OF HORUS)

WARMASTER’S SPITE

When a friendly unit containing one or more models with the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule
declares a Charge against an enemy unit which has had one or more models removed as casualties as a
result of a Shooting Attack made by a model with the Legiones Auxilia (Sons of Horus) special rule in the
same Game Turn, the Charging unit adds +2 to the result of the Charge Distance rolled.

                                  LEGIONES AUXILIA (WORD BEARERS)

CULT DEMAGOGUES

All models in a unit entirely composed of models with both the Legiones Auxilia (Word Bearers) and is part of
a Tercio gain the Fleet and Crusader special rules for the duration of any of the controlling player’s turns in
which at least a single model from the unit begins that turn within 12" of any friendly model with the Legiones
Astartes (Word Bearers) special rule.

                                  LEGIONES AUXILIA (RAVEN GUARD)

SPEARHEAD OF LIBERATION

When a unit entirely composed of models with the Legiones Auxilia (Raven Guard) special rule contains at
least a single model which can draw line of sight to a friendly model within 6" which has the Legiones Astartes
(Raven Guard) special rule and is drawn from the same Army’s Primary Detachment, then all models in the
unit gain the Fearless special rule.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
