        <ns0:categoryLink id="3905cf14-eff3-5296-ab77-4d7c37d0754d" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="989ea28b-4c04-5ba4-b2fe-bf1fb00cccbb" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 45-46" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 45
THE CULTS ABOMINATIO
A single Cult Operative from the Cults Abominatio Army List profile detailed in this section may be included in any Traitor
Detachment. A Cult Operative uses up a Force Organisation slot as normal, but is unaffected by the 'Levels of Alliance
rules and all friendly models in the same army treat it as if it was a Distrusted Ally.

                        Infernus Abomination – 130 Points – Elites Choice
WS        BS        S         T       W        I         A         LD

 5        4         4         4       3        5         4         10

UNIT TYPE – Infantry (Character)                                   UNIT COMPOSITION

                                                         1 Infernus Abomination

WARGEAR                                                            SPECIAL RULES

     •    Transmutative Armaments                        Fearless
     •    Wraithskin                                     Scout
     •    Boneshard Splitter                             Infiltrate
                                                         Abomination
                                                         Adamantium Will
                                                         Fear
                                                         Osmeotic Regeneration
                                                         Empyreal Shift
                                                         Traitor

CULTS ABOMINATIO Special Rules

EMPYREAL SHIFT

Once per enemy turn, the operative may make a special move. This may be made either in the Movement phase whenever
an enemy unit ends its move within 12" of a model with this special rule, in the Shooting phase whenever an enemy unit
targets a model with this special rule with a Shooting Attack, or in the Assault phase whenever an enemy unit declares a
Charge against a unit with this special rule. The controlling player of the model with this special rule must make a
Leadership test. If the Leadership test is passed, the unit with this special rule may immediately move up to 12". This
move may be made in any direction and ignores all terrain or other effects that would limit or modify the distance moved
(including allowing models in the unit to move across Impassable Terrain), as long as the final position of this unit is at
least 1" away from any enemy model and not within an area of Impassable Terrain. If, after moving, the unit that made this
special move is now positioned out of range or line of sight of the unit that caused the move, that unit may not select
another target for the Shooting Attack or Charge that triggered this special rule and no dice are rolled (weapons with the
Gets Hot special rule do not need to roll to see if the weapon Gets Hot and weapons with the One Use special rule are not
considered to have been expended). If the Leadership test is failed, both the unit with this special rule and the unit that
triggered this special rule suffer D6 Wounds with no Armour Saves, Invulnerable Saves or Damage Mitigation rolls
allowed.

ABOMINATION

• Gains Move Through Cover

• Models with this rule never join or be joined by a unit made up of models with any type

. • Models with this rule not Embark on any model with the Transport Sub-type.

• Models with this rule may never be selected as an army's Warlord.

PAGE 46
Osmeotic Regeneration

At the end of the controlling player's turn, if the Infernus Abomination has not been removed as a casualty, the controlling
player rolls a D6 for every unsaved Wound inflicted on an enemy model during that turn. For each result of a 5+, the
Infernus Abomination regains a lost Wound. Note that Wounds regained in this way may not increase the amount of
Wounds to more than the starting amount shown on the Infernus Abomination unit profile.

Boneshard Spitter

Range     S         AP        TYPE

6’        1         -         Assault 2D6, Fleshbane



Transmutative Armaments

Before any To Hit rolls are made during the Assault phase, the controlling player must select which weapon profile lo use.

                                        Range     S        AP      TYPE

                    Hammerblade         -         8        2       Melee, Murderous Strike, Two-Handed

                    Spinelash           -         5        4       Melee, Rending, Reach, Two -Handed

                    Talon-rakes         -         4        5       Melee, Shred, Rending, rampage, Specialist Weapon



Reach

The model with this special rule fights at +1 Initiative



Wraithskin

Models with wraithskin have a 4+ Armour Save and a 4+ Invulnerable Save.</ns0:description>
