    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="af8d3f5e-ed32-5403-8238-78522ece4e8a" name="Legiones Hereticus — Emperor’s Children" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="3103d214-533c-53c0-9d77-26e62997305a" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="e26d9727-7166-5d5c-8a4a-11b991e1353b" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 59-65" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 59
LEGIONES HERETICUS

A Space Marine Legiones Astartes army belonging to the traitor faction may choose to play as a Legiones Hereticus
version of their respective legion if their Daemon Primarch is available. Currently that would be the Emperor’s Children,
Thousand Sons, Word Bearers and Sons of Horus. The following Factions may choose to replace their Legiones Astartes
special rule with the Legiones Hereticus special rule. Space marine models ONLY replace the legions Astartes special
rule, meaning they lose the ability to not be required to roll double 1’s when taking a regroup test when reduced to below
25% starting strength. They still keep all of their other special rules associated with the variant of the Legiones Astartes
special rule unless otherwise stated. For example; a Legiones Hereticus Emperors Children model would keep the
Exemplars of war, Flawless Execution and Martial Pride special rules, but replace the Legiones Astartes special rule with
their legion specific Legiones Hereticus special rule.

Playing any games with Legiones Hereticus means that it is a “Late Heresy” game, so Psykarna should be available and
certain things that are classified only for “Early” Heresy games would not be able to be used. Another note is that Ferrus
Mannus would be dead and cannot be used against any Legiones Hereticus army. Unless players agree of course.

Corrupted Rites of War

Any Detachment that has the Legiones Hereticus Faction, regardless of the specific variant of that Faction (i.e., Legiones
Hereticus (Emperor's Children) or Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Homs), and fulfils at least one of the following conditions
may use a Corrupted Rite of War:

The Detachment includes at least one model with both the Legiones Hereticus special rule and the Master of the Legion
special rule (such as one of the Daemon Primarchs, a Legion Praetor or Legion Centurion with the Delegatus Consul
upgrade). Legiones Hereticus models with the Master of the Legion special rule as well as Daemon Primarchs may still
select any other Rite of War unless there are certain restrictions of course. In any of the other Rites of war, Daemon
Primarchs count as their non transfigured versions and count as primarchs for all intents and purposes.

PAGE 60
Legiones Hereticus – Emperor’s Children
Emperor’s Children models replace their Legion Astartes special rule with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor’s
Children) which grants them the Lords of Profligacy special rule.

LEGIONES HERETICUS (EMPEROR'S CHILDREN) All models with this special rule are subject to the
following provisions:

LORDS OF PROFLIGACY

After a Shooting Attack has been resolved against a unit composed entirely of models with this special rule, it
must take a leadership test, if fails the unit becomes Stupefied if passed nothing happens. A unit can always
choose to fail this test.

If a unit becomes Stupefied while Pinned or affected by the Blind or Concussive special rules, it ignores the
effects of these while Stupefied. Stupefied A unit that is Stupefied can only fire Snap Shots. If a unit that is
Stupefied has a Charge declared for it, then that Charge is always considered to be Disordered. Furthermore,
whilst Stupefied, all models in that unit increase their Strength Characteristic by +1 and when a model in a
Stupefied unit suffers an unsaved Wound, it can make a special Stupefied roll to ignore it. Stupefied rolls may
not be taken against attacks that have the Instant Death special rule. Roll a D6 each time an unsaved Wound
is suffered. On a 6+, the unsaved Wound is ignored. On any other result the Wound is applied as normal. Add i
to Stupefied rolls made for units which have the Fearless special rule. A Stupefied roll is a Damage Mitigation
roll - any model may make only a single Damage Mitigation roll of any type for any given Wound. At the end of
its controlling player's following turn, the unit is no longer Stupefied. Whilst it is Stupefied, a unit does not
take further Morale checks in the Movement phase or Shooting phase and cannot be Pinned. If the unit is
forced to move, for example, if it has to Fall Back, it is no longer Stupefied. If assaulted, the unit will fight as
usual but enemy units do not receive the Initiative penalty for having Charged a unit through Difficult Terrain,
even if the Stupefied unit is in Difficult Terrain. If a unit becomes Stupefied while making a Charge, then that
Charge continues as normal, but is automatically counted as Disordered. Units that are locked in combat can
be Stupefied but take Morale checks in the Assault phase as normal and if forced to Fall Back are no longer
Stupefied.

THE DIVINE INSTRUMENTS

Models with this special rule cannot purchase Sonic Shriekers, instead they may Wargear options from the
The Armoury of Indulgence.

THE PHOENICIAN'S HUBRIS

Phoenix Terminator Squad units with this special rule replace the Living Icons and Phoenix Retinue special
rules with the Fallen From Grace special rule.

Fallen From Grace

A unit with this special rule gains +I to the score used to calculate the winner of a combat during the Assault
phase if it is within 6" of another friendly unit with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule. If
it is within 6" of Fulgrim Transfigured, it instead gains +2 to this score

PAGE 61
THE ARMOURY OF INDULGENCE

The following comprises a list of new options and Wargear available only to Detachments with the Legiones
Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule and exemplifies the nature of that Legion.

DEBASED AUGMENTS

Any model with the Traitor Allegiance and both the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) that has access
to Sonic Shriekers may instead purchase a single upgrade presented here for the same points cost. lf a unit
with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule has an option to give all models in that unit a
Sonic Shrieker, they cannot take them but can instead take a Debased Augment for the additional points
value listed in that unit entry. Each Model in the unit must take the same Debased Augment.

Warp Scream - A model with a warp scream gains the Hammer of Wrath special rule. If the model already
has the Hammer of Wrath special then their Hammer of Wrath attack gains the Rending special rule.

Abhorrent Sensoria - A model with this upgrade gains the Precision Shots and Precision Strikes special rules.

Sublingual Glands - A model with this upgrade gains the sublingual glands weapon:

RANGE            S       AP       TYPE

Template                 -        5       Assault 1, Fleshbane, Blind

PAGE 62
CORRUPTED RITE OF WAR:
                                  BROTHERHOOD OF THE PHOENIX
A Detachment using this Corrupted Rite of War may take up to five HQ choices, regardless of the Force Organisation chart
in use. Each of these HQ choices must be from the following list:

- Lord Commander Eidolon.

- Captain Lucius.

- A Legion Centurion with the Legion Champion Consul upgrade

A Legion Champion in a Detachment using this Corrupted Rite of War gains the Sycophantic Retinue special rule.

SYCOPHANTIC RETINUE

While Fulgrim Transfigured is on the battlefield, models with this special rule gain the Preferred Enemy (Everything)
special rule.

Limitations of War.

• Fulgrim Transfigured must be included in a Detachment using this Corrupted Rite




                                        CORRUPTED RITE OF WAR:
                                    CHILDREN OF THE MARAVIGLIA
All models in a unit from an Allied Detachment gain the Stubborn special rule while at least one model from that unit is
within 6" of any model with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule in the same army.

Fulgrim Transfigured gains the The Stage is Set special rule.

Limitations

• Fulgrim Transfigured must be included in a Detachment using this Corrupted Rite of War.

• This Rite of War may only be selected for a Primary Detachment.

• An army whose Primary Detachment is using this Rite of War must include an Allied Detachment that is selected from
the Solar Auxilia or lmperialis Militia Army Lists that includes at least four units.

THE STAGE IS SET

Before the start of the first turn, when placing units into Reserves, the controlling player may place Fulgrim Transfigured
into Reserves and must declare to their opponent a Turn number from Turn 2 - 4, indicating on which of their own turns
they will bring Fulgrin1 Transfigured into play from Reserves. At the start of the declared turn, the controlling player must
place Fulgrim Transfigured wholly within 6" of a unit with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule, and
not within 1" of any enemy models. If this is not possible, Fulgrim Transfigured cannot be set up this turn, and the
controlling player must attempt to deploy Fulgrim Transfigured again at the start of their following turn. Until Fulgrim
Transfigured is placed on the battlefield in this manner, all models in a Detachment he is part of have the Stubborn
special rule.

PAGE 63
Fulgrim Transfigured............................................600 Points – LORD OF WAR CHOICE
          WS        BS        S         T           W      I         A         LD

          8         6         7         7           7      8         7         10



UNIT TYPE – Flying Monstrous Creature (Character)                    UNIT COMPOSITION

                                                                               1 (Unique)



WARGEAR                                                              SPECIAL RULES

• Blades of the Pheonician                                           Daemon

• Serpentine Daemonform                                              Scion of Corruption (Emperor’s Children)

                                                                     Sublime Swordsman

                                                                     Psyker (Mastery level 2)

                                                                     Warlord: Avatar of Perfection

                                                                     Primarch (Eternal warrior, Adamantium Will, Fleet,
                                                                     Fearless, It Will Not Die, Master of the Legion, Precision
                                                                     strikes, Precision Shots.)

Warlord Trait – Avatar of Perfection:

If chosen as the army's Warlord, Fulgrim Transfigured automatically has the Avatar of Perfection Warlord Trait and may not
select any other Warlord Trait.

Avatar of Perfection - During the controlling player's Charge sub-phase, Fulgrim Transfigured must attempt a Charge if
there are any enemy units that contain any models with an unmodified Weapon Skill characteristic of 6 or more within 12",
and at least one of these enemy units must be declared as a target of that Charge. Note that this does allow a unit that
contains a model with this Warlord Trait to Charge a different unit to one that they made a Shooting Attack against in the
previous Shooting phase. In the subsequent Fight sub-phase, the controlling player must issue a Challenge, and must
nominate Fulgrim to be the Challenger. If the Challenge is accepted by an enemy model with a Weapon Skill
characteristic of 6, while that Challenge is ongoing, Attacks made for Fulgrim Transfigured hit on a result of 2+, regardless
of the Weapon Skill characteristic of the target.

Serpentine Daemonform - provides a 2+ Armour Save and a 4+ Invulnerable Save. Additionally, while Fulgrim
Transfigured has four or fewer wounds, add +1 to dice rolls made for his It Will Not Die Special Rule. If, at the start of any
of their player turns, Fulgrim Transfigured has two or fewer Wounds and is not locked in combat, his controlling player
may choose to remove Fulgrim Transfigured from play as a casualty. If Fulgrim Transfigured is removed from play in this
manner, the opposing player achieves no Objectives or Secondary Objectives that would otherwise be scored by
removing Fulgrim Transfigured as a casualty.

PAGE 64
Blades of the Phoenician - At the start of each combat, Fulgrim Transfigured's controlling player must choose one of the
following profiles to use:

Decapitating Slashes

         S         AP        TYPE

         User      2         Melee, Instant Death

Sundering Blows

         S         AP        TYPE

         +3        2         Melee, Wrathful Blows, Instant Death, Unwieldy




Wrathful Blows: A model making Attacks with this weapon makes 3 attacks with it only. Regardless of their Attacks
Characteristic and any bonuses gained for Charging and for the sublime swordsman special rule.

 Scion of Corruption (Emperor’s Children) - All units with the Legiones Astartes (Emperor's Children) special rule in an
army that includes Fulgrim Transfigured must replace it with the Legiones Hereticus (Emperor's Children) special rule.
You also cannot include Fulgrim Transfigured in the same army as Fulgrim. Fulgrim Transfigured is Psyker with a mastery
level of 2 and can only generate powers from the Discipline of Excess from the Chaos Daemons book which is included in
these rules. Furthermore, Fulgrim Transfigured counts as being able to use the Lords of Profligacy special rule. Fulgrim
Transfigured counts as a Daemon of Slaanesh as well, meaning that all of his attacks have the Rending special rule and
can always run an additional 3”.

Sublime Swordsman:

In an assault, Fulgrim’s invulnerable save is increased to 3+. In addition, when fighting in a challenge, he gains a number
of additional attacks equal to the amount which his initiative value is greater than that of his opponent so, for example, if
he fights a model with an initiative value of 5, Fulgrim’s initiative of 8 grants him 3 extra attacks.

PAGE 65
DISCIPLINE OF EXCESS
Primaris — Lash of Slaanesh (Warp Charge 1): Beam; Range 24", S6 AP-, Assault 1, Rending.
1 Acquiescence (WC1): Malediction, enemy within 18"; -5 Initiative (minimum 1), cannot Counter-attack or Overwatch while active.
2 Pavane of Slaanesh (WC1): Focused Witchfire, Range 24"; target takes a Leadership test; if failed suffers one Wound with no Armour or Cover save. If slain, randomly select another model in the unit and repeat until a test is passed or the unit is destroyed.
3 Maniacal Fervour (WC1): Blessing, friendly unit within 24"; immediately suffers D6 S3 AP- hits; while active gains Furious Charge, Rage and Zealot.
4 Phantasmagoria (WC1): Malediction, enemy within 18"; whenever it attempts to move, manifest, Run, shoot, charge, attack, fight, Sweep, Consolidate or Overwatch, it must first pass a Leadership test or cannot perform that action. A failed action does not prevent a different action later in the phase, which requires a separate test.
5 Slicing Shards (WC2): Witchfire; Range 24", S4 AP4, Assault 1, Large Blast, Soul Flay. Soul Flay: after resolving the blast, units wholly or partially under it take a Leadership test or suffer D6 S4 AP4 hits.
6 Cacophonic Choir (WC2): Nova, Range 12"; each target rolls 2D6 and subtracts Leadership, suffering that many Wounds with no Armour or Cover saves, then takes a Pinning test.</ns0:description>
