    <ns0:selectionEntry id="1d3a1565-0839-50b8-935d-bf7443037619" name="Legiones Hereticus — Thousand Sons" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="c3f7bc46-d7a4-594e-b0bd-139a9857f088" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="d2718bdf-bf76-5440-9b4f-fe057fded5e0" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 66-71" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 66
LEGIONES HERETICUS (THOUSAND SONS)
Thousand Sons models replace their Legion Astartes special rule with Legiones Hereticus (Thousand Sons)
which grants them the LORDS OF FALLEN PROSPERO special rule.



LEGIONES HERETICUS (Thousand Sons) All models with this special rule are subject to the following
provisions:



LORDS OF FALLEN PROSPERO: This special rule provides the following rules for all models with the Legiones
Hereticus (Thousand Sons) special rule. Each unit with this special rule still retains all of the rules such as
Covenant of Sorcerers, Prosperine Lore, Cult Arcana and Signs and Portents

DUST BOUND

All non Psyker models with the Legiones Hereticus (Thousand Sons) special rule gain the slow and purposeful
special rule and automatically pass all morale and regroup tests. They also cannot be pinned unless by the
Signs and Portents special rule. They must pass a successful Leadership test in order to declare a charge
unless a Psyker is present in the unit.

THE SORCEROR COMMANDS

All eligible units cease to have the Brotherhood of Psykers special rule – instead only the squad leader in each
respective squad would have the Psyker special rule. Ahriman cannot be included in a Legiones Hereticus
Army that also includes Magnus the Red Transfigured and Magistus Amon may not be included at all.

In addition, Thousand Sons Legion Tactical squads may not be taken. Instead Thousand Sons Legion Inductii
squads lose the support squad special rule and may be taken as compulsory troops choices in the place of
Tactical Marines.

(***BOON OF FLAME RULE CHANGE****)

Because Daemons of the Ruinstorm exists and not Chaos Daemons, the following rules replaces the text for Boon of Flame (For Magnus
Transfigured only)

Boon of flame is a Conjuration power with a range of 12”. If you manifest this power at Mastery Level 2, it creates a single Ruinstorm
Daemon Chosen. Alternateively you can decide to attempt to manifest this power at Warp Charge 3 (Decide before rolling). If you do so,
you can instead choose to create one of the following units: 3 Ruinstorm Daemon Calvary or a single Ruinstorm Daemon Beast.

PAGE 67
Magnus the Red Transfigured............................................650 Points – LORD OF WAR CHOICE

          WS        BS        S         T           W      I           A        LD

          7         7         8         7           7      7           6         10



UNIT TYPE – Flying Monstrous Creature (Character)                      UNIT COMPOSITION

                                                                                1 (Unique)

WARGEAR                                                                SPECIAL RULES

• The Blade of Magnus                                                  Daemon

• Crown of the Crimson King                                            Scion of Corruption (Thousand Sons)

                                                                       Omniscient Eye

                                                                       Unearthly Power

                                                                       Psyker (Mastery level 5)

                                                                       Warlord: Lord of Flux

                                                                       Primarch (Eternal warrior, Adamantium Will, Fleet,
                                                                       Fearless, It Will Not Die, Master of the Legion, Precision
                                                                       strikes, Precision Shots.)

Warlord Trait: Lord of Flux - Enemy units within 12" of your Warlord treat all terrain, even open ground, as difficult terrain.
In addition, all models in any enemy units that Run, Turbo-boost, move Flat Out or charge within 12" of your Warlord must
take a Dangerous Terrain test

WARGEAR

The Blade of Magnus

          S         AP        TYPE

          User      2         Melee, Force, Soul Blaze, Transmogrify




Transmogrify: Any To Wound roll of 6 made by an attack that has this special rule gains the Instant Death special rule. If
any models are slain in this manner, then you may immediately place a new Chaos Spawn model under your control as
close as possible to where any of the slain models were standing, but more than 1" from any enemy models.

Crown of the Crimson King: Magnus the Red Transfigured has a 4+ invulnerable save and never suffers from Perils of the
Warp.

PAGE 68
Special Rules

Scion of Corruption (Thousand Sons):

All units with the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule in an army that includes Magnus the Red
Transfigured must replace it with the Legiones Hereticus (Thousand Sons) special rule. You also cannot
include Magnus the Red Transfigured in the same army as Magnus the Red. Magnus the Red Transfigured is a
psyker with a master level of 5 and knows the Gaze of Magnus psychic power as well as all of the powers from
the Tzeentch and Change disciplines. When Magnus is the Warlord, no restrictions owing to Cult Arcana
applies to the compulsory units of the army. Magnus the Red transfigured also counts as a Daemon of
Tzeentch meaning that he can reroll saving throws of 1. In addition, when Magnus is affected by a Blessing
type psychic power, he improves his invulnerable save by 1.

Omniscient Eye: Magnus has line of sight to every unit on the battlefield when determining the targets of his
psychic powers.

Unearthly Power: Magnus harnesses Warp Charge points on a result of 2+ when attempting to manifest
psychic powers



Chaos Spawn (For the Transmogrify special rule)



        WS       BS      S        T       W        I       A        LD

        3        0       5        5       3        3       D6       10



UNIT TYPE – Beast                                          UNIT COMPOSITION – 1 Chaos Spawn

WARGEAR - None                                                      SPECIAL RULES

                                                           Random Attacks

                                                           Mutated Beyond Reason

Random Attacks: At the beginning of each Fight sub-phase, roll a D6 for each Chaos Spawn unit locked in
combat. The Result is the number of attacks (before modifiers) that all chaos spawn in that unit have this
turn.

Mutated Beyond Reason: At the beginning of each Fight sub-phase, before rolling for their Random Attacks,
roll a D3 on the table below for each friendly Chaos Spawn unit that is locked in combat. The mutation affects
every Chaos Spawn model in the unit and lasts for the rest of the turn

1 – Subcutaneous Armor – The Chaos Spawn have an armor save of 4+

2 – Grasping Pseudopods – The Chaos Spawn unit rolls two D6 and picks the highest for their Random Attacks

3 – Toxic Hemorrhage – The Chaos Spawns attacks have the Poisoned special rule

PAGE 69
DISCIPLINE OF CHANGE
Primaris — Flickering Fire of Tzeentch (WC1–3): Witchfire. Choose Warp Charge 1, 2 or 3; each additional point adds D6 shots after the first. Range 24", S5 AP4, Assault 2D6, Soul Blaze, Warpflame.
1 Tzeentch's Firestorm (WC1): Witchfire, 24", S D6+1 AP-, Assault 1, Blast, Warpflame.
2 Bolt of Change (WC1): Beam, 24", S D6+4 AP2, Assault 1, Warpflame.
3 Tzeentch's Warpflare (WC1): Nova, 9", S D6 AP4, Assault 2D6, Ignores Cover, Warpflame.
4 Boon of Flame (WC2–3): Conjuration within 12"; WC2 creates one Exalted Flamer of Tzeentch; WC3 creates either three Flamers or one Burning Chariot. (The Thousand Sons Hereticus page replaces this effect for Magnus the Red Transfigured with Ruinstorm equivalents.)
5 Infernal Gateway (WC2): Witchfire, 18", S D6+4 AP1, Assault 1, Blast, Warpflame.
6 Prismatic Gaze (WC3): Witchfire, 18", S D AP1, Assault 1.
Warpflame: at the end of each phase, a unit that suffered one or more unsaved Wounds from Warpflame takes a Toughness test. If failed it suffers D3 Wounds with no Armour or Cover saves. If passed, all models gain Feel No Pain (6+) for the rest of the game, or improve existing Feel No Pain by 1.

PAGE 70
DISCIPLINE OF TZEENTCH
Primaris — Tzeentch's Firestorm (WC1): Witchfire, 24", S D6+1 AP-, Assault 1, Blast, Inferno. Inferno: each casualty caused inflicts an additional D3 S3 AP- hits; these extra hits do not generate more hits.
1 Boon of Mutation (WC1): Blessing on one friendly Character within 2"; suffers S4 AP- hit, and if it survives rolls on the Chaos Boon table, re-rolling Dark Apotheosis.
2 Doombolt (WC1): Beam, 18", S8 AP1, Assault 1, Detonate. If it hits a vehicle and causes Explodes, roll 2D6 for explosion range.
3 Siphon Magic (WC1): Blessing on self; for the rest of the phase each friendly model within 18" that successfully manifests a psychic power contributes a bonus Warp Charge die to this Psyker.
4 Breath of Chaos (WC2): Witchfire, Template, S1 AP2, Assault 1, Corrosion, Poisoned (4+). Corrosion: vehicles touched suffer a Glancing Hit on 4+ instead of normal armour penetration.
5 Baleful Devolution (WC2): Focused Witchfire, 18", S6 AP2, Assault D6, Transmogrify. On a To Wound roll of 6, Instant Death; a model slain is replaced by a Chaos Spawn as described.
6 Treason of Tzeentch (WC3): Malediction on enemy non-vehicle unit within 24" not locked in combat. Immediately make a Shooting Attack with every model as though friendly and stationary, then the unit takes a Pinning test.
Gaze of Magnus (WC5): Beam, 18", S D AP1, Assault 1, Soul Blaze.

PAGE 71
CORRUPTED RITES OF WAR
REHATI WAR SECT


A Detachment using this Corrupted Rite of War may take up to five HQ choices and each of them must
either be Praetors with Mastery Level 3, or Consuls with the Librarian or Esoterist upgrade (ignoring the
support officer special rule).

Each HQ choice selected in this manor gains the following special rule:

Court of the Crimson King: Whilst they are within 18" of Daemon Primarch Magnus the Red, all HQ choice
psykers reroll 1s when harnessing Warp Charges. In addition, they have line of sight to every unit on the
battlefield when determining the targets of their psychic powers.

There be magick here: When generating Warp Charges at the start of any psychic phase, the controlling
player adds the following effect to the dice roll. On a 1, a random Psyker unit takes a perils of the warp
immediately. On a 6, the controlling player gains D3 warp charge points for this psychic phase.



Restrictions -

-all HQ choice psykers must be upgraded to have the max amount of Mastery Levels possible.

-Magnus the Red Transfigured must be taken and is the Warlord




THE RED COVENANT


All models in a unit from an Allied Detachment gain the following special rules

Avaricious Vigour: non vehicle units from chosen from the Militia &amp; warp cults that are within 18” of Daemon
Primarch Magnus gain the fleet special rule, in addition if a charging unit rolls a 9 or more for its charge, they
gain +1 strength for that turn until the beginning of the next player turn.

Warp Conduits: Add one dice to your Warp Charge pool in each Psychic phase for each non vehicle unit
within 18” of Magnus the Red Transfigured from the allied detachment that is on the battlefield

Restrictions:

- Must take an allied detachment from the militia &amp; warp cults of at least 4 units.

- Abhuman Helots and Tainted Flesh must be the provenances chosen

- Magnus the Red Transfigured must be included and is the Warlord

- Can only use this Rite of War as the Primary detachment</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
