        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="0ece1e95-b29c-5964-b374-ca88d63cac94" name="Legiones Hereticus — Word Bearers" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="4bcff85f-f121-5a18-99f4-f2dced42cdb4" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="afafc277-b0fd-5f5c-8433-1715097cd9e8" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 72-73" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 72
LEGIONES HERETICUS (WORD BEARERS)
Word Bearers models replace their Legion Astartes special rule with Legiones Hereticus (Word Bearers)
which grants them the DARK CRUSADERS special rule. In Addition, Argel Tal and Gal Vorbak gain the
Legiones Hereticus (Word Bearers) Special rule, meaning that they also gain True believers and Cut Them
Down.

LEGIONES HERETICUS (Word Bearers) All models with this special rule are subject to the following
provisions:

DARK CRUSADERS: Models with this special rule subject to the following:

    -    They gain the Crusader Special rule.
    -    Any unit that can take Dark Channeling MUST take it
    -    Any model with Access to Burning lore can instead take a Malefic Power. Models that suffer from
         perils of the warp in a Legiones Hereticus Word Bearers when attempting to manifest warp charges
         may reroll the result on the perils of the warp table. The second roll must be accepted.
    -    Argel Tal may take a Legio Custodes Guardian Spear.

Guardian Spear with inbuilt Guardian Bolter

         RANGE        S             AP       TYPE

         -        As User/+1*       3/2*     Melee, Lightning Blows, Specialist Weapon

         18”          4             4        Assault 2



         *Use the second profile if the model has charged this turn



                  Lightning Blows: Every roll of a 6 to hit with this weapon generates another attack with the
                  same weapon at the same initiative step. These extra attacks do not generate additional
                  attacks

Argel Tal also has the following special rules:

Argel Tal is now Infantry.

Resplendent Wings: At the beginning of the controlling player’s turn, Argel Tal may change his type to Jump
infantry. This effect last until the beginning of the next players turn. Argel Tal must be on the table and not in a
transport in order for this to take effect.

PAGE 73
Corrupted Rites of War
The Dark Council
The Anointed: A single Legion Terminator Squad must be chosen as an additional Compulsory Troops
choice, in addition to the normal compulsory choices. This single Legion Terminator Squad gains the
following special rules: +1 Toughness, +1 Invulnerable save, +1 Initiative and the Rage Special rule.

The Voice of Lorgar: At the start of each of your turns, pick one of the following special rules to bestow upon
a single unit from a Word Bearers Detachment that is within 12" of Lorgar Transfigured: Counter-attack,
Fearless, Furious Charge, Relentless. The unit you pick gains that special rule until the start of your next turn

Lords of Darkness: Lorgar Transfigured must be included and counts as a Lord of War detachment and up to
5 HQ choices may be chosen. HQ choices selected in this manor must have the Zealot Special rule or have
the Diabolist Consul type upgrade.

Limitations:

No fortifications

Only allies allowed to be used are Daemons of the Ruinstorm or Traitor Mechanicum.



Shepherds of the Lost and the Damned
This Rite of War is to be used in an Army of Dark Compliance, ignoring the restriction that Rites of war
may not be taken in one usually. All of the same restrictions and rules apply.

A Tide of Traitors: Each time a unit of inducted Levy is completely destroyed, roll a D6, on a 4+ you can
immediately place a new, identical unit into Ongoing Reserve. Subsequent units that have been destroyed
again may be rolled for again. These new units gain the Outflank special rule. Victory Points are awarded as
normal for new units that have been completely destroyed.

The Desperate and the Depraved: Units of inducted levy have a Leadership of 10 while they are within 12" of
any Word Bearers independent character model with the Zealot special rule or Lorgar Transfigured.

Chaos Space Marines: Lorgar Transfigured must be taken and counts as an HQ choice for the army. He also
counts as the Force Commander for the army and has the Muster of Worlds special rule. For the purposes of
which army he counts as, he counts as one of each. Units of Daemon Engines (Decimators, Blood
Slaughterers, Brass Scorpion, Kytan) may be taken as their respective unit choices therefore do not count as
either Space Marines or Imperialis militia &amp; Cults, A Legion Praevian is not required to take Daemon Engines



Limitations:

The Provenances chosen must be Cult Horde and Tainted Flesh

No Allies, no Fortifications</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="e81c917f-82f2-5e50-912a-d285bd225a34" name="Legiones Hereticus — Sons of Horus" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="00de1ca3-5a02-5574-aec8-2ed8cf20f6c6" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="7ac29ce7-65ce-543a-95dd-dee053a1d454" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 74-75" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 74
LEGIONES HERETICUS (SONS OF HORUS)
Sons of Horus models replace their Legion Astartes special rule with Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus) which grants
them the ENDLESS HATRED special rule.

Abaddon also now has a Paragon Blade instead of a Power sword.

ENDLESS HATRED: Models with this special rule may reroll 1s to hit in the first round of combat against any army with the Loyalist
faction




                                                      Corrupted Rites of War

The Warmaster’s Shadow
Luperci: Legion Veterans must be taken as compulsory troops choices and instead of selecting a veteran ability, they gain +1 Strength,
Fleet and the Daemon Special Rule.

The Warmaster of Chaos: All Friendly models with the Daemon Special Rule within 12” of Horus Ascended gain Preferred Enemy
(Loyalists)



Limitations:

Must include an Allied Daemons of the Ruinstorm detachment with at least 4 units

No Librarians or Esoterists allowed.

Horus Ascended must be included.

Must be the Primary Detachment




The Warmaster’s Chosen
Mournival: Horus Ascended must be included in this army as a Lord of War choice and the controlling player may choose up to 5 HQ
Choices. However, only models with the Master of the Legion special rule may be chosen as HQ choices.

Thirst for Glory: If an enemy unit is completely destroyed by a unit with the Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus) special rule, all other
units with the Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus) special rule can re-roll To Hit and To Wound rolls of 1 until the end of the phase

Annihilation force: For each HQ choice taken, a Compulsory Troops choice must be taken. In an army with this Corrupted Rite of War,
Legion Reavers, Legion Veterans, Legion Terminators and Legion Justaerin may be chosen as compulsory troops choices in this manor.



Limitations:

No allies, no fortifications

Must be Primary Detachment

Legion Tactical squads, Assault Squads, Breacher squads, Recon Marine Squads and Support Squads may not be taken in this army.

PAGE 75
Hors Ascended Uses all of the rules for regular Horus from the Legions book from 1.0. His stat line changes to the following and gains a
number of additional rules such as gains Rage, Feel no Pain (4+), A Dark Fate, The Power of Chaos Eternal and The Spreading
Corruption. In addition, Horus Ascended counts as having the Endless Hatred special rule.




   Horus Ascended............................................1000 Points – LORD OF WAR CHOICE
          WS         BS        S          T          W         I          A         LD

           8         6         8          8          8         6          6          10

A Dark Fate

The first time in any battle that Horus Ascended loses his last Wound, or is otherwise removed from play as a casualty, the
model is instead placed into Reserves with a single Wound remaining – any unit Horus Ascended was part of remains in
play, even a Retinue or other unit that would normally not allow the removal of a model from the unit. After having been
placed in Reserves due to this special rule, Horus Ascended may choose to re-enter play, with the controlling player
making Reserves rolls for the model as per the normal rules. If the Slay the Warlord objective, or any other objective that
requires the enemy Warlord be removed as a casualty to score Victory points, is in effect then it is still triggered when
Horus Ascended is moved into Reserves due to this special rule – and may be triggered a second time if Horus Ascended
returns to play and is removed as a casualty again.



The Power of Chaos Eternal

Once per battle, at the start of any Assault phase (whether Horus Ascended’ s controlling player is the Active or Reactive
player), Horus Ascended’ s controlling player may choose to activate the Power of Chaos Eternal. Once activated, Horus
Ascended increases his Strength and Toughness Characteristics to 10 for the duration of the Assault phase and ignores
all the effects of the Unwieldy special rule on attacks made with Worldbreaker. Once the Assault phase is ended, all
combats being fought have been resolved and the effects of the Power of Chaos Eternal have ended, Horus Ascended
automatically suffers Perils of the Warp – but any Wounds caused must be allocated to friendly models in the same unit
as Horus Ascended, if any such models exist, before they are allocated to Horus Ascended.

The Spreading Corruption:

A unit composed entirely of models with the Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus) special fails a Morale check it does not
Fall Back as per the standard rules, but instead suffers D3 automatic Wounds with no saves or Damage Mitigation rolls of
any kind allowed. These wounds are randomly allocated.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="21eca853-30f0-5a50-8e5a-1efde5822422" name="Legiones Inductii" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="4eb978f5-0f88-5928-83f6-2600dd1ffa57" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="4037e51f-9272-5705-bcbd-84d46cc4b0d4" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 76-81" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 76
LEGIONES INDUCTII


LEGIONES ASTARTES INDUCTII TEMPLATES

To represent the Inductii forces within each of the Legions, a system of templates are used to modify certain
unit entries in the Legiones Astartes Army List. Each variation of the Legiones Astartes rule is associated with
a specific Inductii template, representing the specific form and function of Inductii each Legion created and
utilised within their own ranks. These templates are applied to a unit when the unit is chosen during army
selection, before any options are selected for the unit. The modifications that a template applies to a unit are
only applied to the specific unit that it is chosen for. No unit may have more than one template applied to it.
Inductii rules only ever apply to Legion Tactical Squads. Almost all Inductii will have a special rule that
replaces the Fury of the Legion special rule.

INDUCTII TEMPLATE FORMAT

Each Inductii template includes the key information listed below:

• Legiones Astartes (X): Each Inductii template may only be applied to units with a specific variation of the
Legiones Astartes (X) special rule in a detachment with the same variation of the Legiones Astartes (X)
Faction.

• Unit Composition: Some Inductii templates will modify the composition of the unit. This could include the
starting number of models, the inclusion of Sergeants, and the option to take additional models in the unit.

• Wargear: Some Inductii templates will add, remove, or replace Wargear in the base unit entry. If a template
removes or replaces Wargear which can normally be exchanged in the Options of the base unit entry, those
options are no longer available to the unit.

• Special Rules: Some Inductii templates will add, remove, or replace special rules in the base unit entry.



INDUCTII UNITS SPECIAL RULE

The following rules apply to all models with the Inductii Special Rule:

• A unit that includes any models with the Inductii Special Rule cannot be joined by any other models or have
any other models assigned to it.

• No model in a unit that includes any models with the Inductii Special Rule can exchange their power armour
for artificer armour.

• A unit that includes any models with the Inductii Special Rule has the Support Squad special rule.

• A unit that includes any models with the Inductii Special Rule can never purchase extra close combat
weapons

PAGE 77
EMPEROR’S CHILDREN LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Emperor’s Children

• Characteristic Profile: No modification.

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models in this unit must exchange their bolters for a close combat weapon. Any model in a unit
modified by the Emperor’s Children Legion Inductii template may exchange their chainsword for a Charnabal
Blade for +5 points each.

 • Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Emperor’s Children Legion Inductii template must
replace the Fury of the Legion special rule with the Perfection Embodied special rule.

Perfection Embodied:

 All models in a unit with this special rule are considered to have a Leadership Characteristic of 10 when
resolving Morale checks in the Shooting phase or Pinning tests. If a unit with this special rule is part of a
combat that results in a draw, then a side that includes one or more models at the end of the Fight sub-phase
with this special rule is counted as having lost the combat by 1 point. If both sides include models with this
special rule then the combat remains a draw.

                          IRON WARRIORS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Iron Warriors

• Characteristic Profile: No modification.

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models cannot replace their bolter with a close combat weapon.

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Iron Warriors Legion Inductii template must replace the
Fury of the Legion special rule with the Souls of Iron special rule.

Souls of Iron:

During the controlling player’s Shooting phase, a unit with this special rule must attempt a Shooting Attack if
there is an enemy unit within range, and must target the closest enemy unit possible that is within its line of
sight and is a valid target for a Shooting Attack. If two or more targets are equally close then the controlling
player chooses which will be the target of a Shooting Attack. In addition, this unit has the Feel No Pain (6+)
and stubborn special rules if within 6” of an objective.

PAGE 78
SPACE WOLVES LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Space Wolves

• Characteristic Profile: No modification.

• Unit Composition: Replace the Legion Tactical Sergeant of a unit modified by the Space Wolves Legion
Inductii template with one additional Legionary.

• Wargear: Models must replace their bolter with a close combat weapon. All models in a unit modified by
the Space Wolves Legion Inductii template may replace all bolt pistols in the unit with combat shields for no
additional points cost. Any model in a unit modified by the Space Wolves Legion Inductii template may
replace its chainsword with a chainaxe for +1 point per model.

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Space Wolves Legion Inductii template must replace the
Fury of the Legion special rule with the Headstrong special rule.

Headstrong:

When declaring a Charge for a unit composed entirely of models with this special rule, the controlling player
can declare it will be a headstrong charge. If they do so, when rolling to determine the Charge Distance, add 2
to the result and that charge is Disordered (this does not allow units to Charge a total distance of more than
12"

                         IMPERIAL FISTS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Imperial Fists

• Characteristic Profile: No modification.

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models may not replace their Bolters for close combat weapons. For every ten models in a unit
modified by the Imperial Fists Legion Inductii template, one Legionary may exchange his bolter for one of the
following:

- Heavy bolter....................................+10 points per model

- Autocannon.....................................+15 points per model

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Imperial Fists Legion Inductii template must replace the
Fury of the Legion special rule with the Supporting Fire special rule.

Supporting Fire

Once per battle, the controlling player of a unit that includes any models with this special rule may declare a
Supporting Fire before making a Shooting Attack with that unit. Until that Shooting Attack is resolved,
weapons with the Heavy type in that unit gain the Pinning special rule in addition to any other effects their
weapons might have

PAGE 79
IRON HANDS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Iron Hands

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: The unit may not replace their bolters with close combat weapons and the squad gains Hardened
Armor, In addition, The Legion Tactical Sergeant in a unit modified by the Iron Hands Legion Inductii template
may take one phosphex bomb for +10 points.

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Iron Hands Legion Inductii template replace the Fury of
the Legion special rule with the Forbidden Augmentations special rule.

Forbidden Augmentations:

At the start of the controlling player’s turn as the Active player, before the beginning of the Movement phase,
roll one dice for each unit that includes one or more models with this special rule. On the roll of a 5+, all
models in that unit with this special rule gain +1 WS and +1 BS until the end of that player turn, however, on
the roll of a 1 or 2 the unit suffer D3 Wounds with an AP value of ‘-’, allocated by the unit’s controlling player. In
addition, this unit may not run.



                            ULTRAMARINES LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Ultramarines

• Unit Composition: A unit modified by the Ultramarines Legion Inductii template may not take additional
Legionaries.

• Wargear: Models may not replace their bolters with close combat weapons. For every five models in the
unit modified by the Ultramarines Legion Inductii template, one Legionary may exchange his bolter for one of
the following:

- Flamer ........................................................+5 points each

- Plasma gun ..............................................+15 points each

- Meltagun...................................................+15 points each

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Ultramarines Legion Inductii template replace the Fury
of the Legion special rule with the Inexorable special rule.

Inexorable:

Models with this special rule ignore all negatives to Leadership tests and Pinning tests.

PAGE 80
THOUSAND SONS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Thousand Sons

• Unit Composition: The Sergreant is upgraded to have the Psyker Mastery level 1 special rule and must
replace their Close Combat weapon with a Force Stave for 15 points.

• Wargear: Models in a unit modified by the Thousand Sons Legion Inductii template cannot exchange their
bolters for close combat weapons

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Thousand Sons Inductii template replace the Fury of the
Legion special rule with the Unattuned Practitioners special rule

Unattuned Practitioners – If this unit ever suffers from Perils of the warp, roll 2 D6 and apply the lowest
result. The Psyker knows the Ætheric Guidance Psychic Power. It is not aided in any way by cult arcana
special rules.

Ætheric Guidance – Blessing – Warp Charge 2

This is a Blessing that targets the Psyker and his unit. While this blessing is active, shooting attacks made by
this unit have the Rending special rule.



                     SONS OF HORUS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Sons of Horus

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models must replace their bolter for a close combat weapon. Any model in a unit modified by the
Sons of Horus Legion Inductii template may replace its chainsword with a chainaxe for +1 point per model.

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Sons of Horus Legion Inductii template replace the Fury
of the Legion special rule with the Creed of Brutality special rule

Creed of Brutality

At the start of each Assault phase, if a unit that includes at least one model with this special rule has any
models within 6" of a friendly model with the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule that has a
Weapon Skill characteristic of 5 or more, all models in the unit with this special rule gain the Rampage and
Furious Charge special rules until the end of that Phase.

PAGE 81
WORD BEARERS LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Word Bearers

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models must replace their bolters with close combat weapons.

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Word Bearers Legion Inductii template replace the Fury
of the Legion special rule with the Empty Vessels Special rules.

Empty Vessels

Models with this special rule may not be given the Dark Channeling special rule unless it is gained through
this special rule. At the end of each Game Turn, the controlling player of a unit with this special rule rolls a D6
for each unit with this special rule. Add 1 to the result if any enemy units were destroyed as a result of an
attack or sweeping advance made by that unit during this Game Turn and add 1 to the result if the enemy
Warlord has been destroyed during the battle. On a 5+, that unit suffers D3 wounds with an AP value of ‘-’ and
gains Dark Channeling. Roll on the Dark Channeling table and apply the result immediately.




                       RAVEN GUARD LEGION INDUCTII TEMPLATE
• Legiones Astartes: Raven Guard

• Unit Composition: No modification.

• Wargear: Models may not replace their Bolters with close combat weapons

• Special Rules: All models in a unit modified by the Raven Guard Legion Inductii template replace the Fury
of the Legion special rule with the Unchained Conviction special rule.

Unchained Conviction: Once per turn, whenever a unit composed entirely of models with this special rule
becomes pinned either through failing a pinning test or going to ground it is instead not Pinned and instead
must immediately move 6" directly away from the enemy unit that caused the Pinning test, moving each
model in the unit directly away from that enemy unit by the shortest available path, ignoring any terrain except
for impassable terrain. The Raven Guard unit making this move receives any damage first before making this
move. They do not receive the benefit of being pinned when using this special rule. If this would bring the unit
into contact with the edge of the battlefield, do not move it any further. Once all models in the unit have been
moved, there are no further effects and the unit is not Pinned.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="6d314364-cbb4-5f0c-88ba-f26fc3a5f8e1" name="Solar Auxilia Cohort Doctrines" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="c9584246-8101-5f66-ae1c-022faa5103a0" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="4dfddc56-08f8-57d7-b0be-da742af0969a" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="ca0608cf-2680-5e73-b40b-2a5e4fd44223" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 82-86" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 82
SOLAR AUXILIA COHORT DOCTRINES
Each Cohort Doctrine presents one of the unique styles of war mastered by a cohort of the Solar Auxilia, and
is chosen when a player Solar Auxilia Cohort Doctrines selects their army – before the start of a battle. The
rules for each individual Cohort Doctrine will present a number of Effects which will grant the Detachment
new options or special rules, as well as a number of Limitations which will deny the Detachment access to
certain options or rules it might otherwise be able to make use of. Unless otherwise stated as part of the
Cohort Doctrine’ s rules, all Effects and Limitations must be applied to models and units that are selected as
part of the Detachment that it has been chosen for.

The Effects and Limitations of any given Cohort Doctrine only apply to units and models in the Detachment it
was chosen for – unless the Cohort Doctrine specifically states otherwise. Where more than one Detachment
in an army is eligible to choose a Cohort Doctrine (i.e., has the Solar Auxilia Faction, and includes at least one
model with the Cohort Doctrines special rule), each Detachment may select a Cohort Doctrine – unless one
of those Cohort Doctrines includes a limitation that requires the player not to select additional Cohort
Doctrines. Some Cohort Doctrines may only be chosen for a Primary Detachment or an Allied Detachment,
such Limitations will be clearly stated as part of the Cohort Doctrine.

Gaining Access to Cohort Doctrines

LEGATE COMMANDERS AND LORD MARSHALS AS WELL AS LORD MARSHAL IRETON MASADE GAIN THE
COHORT DOCTRINES SPECIAL RULE

Any Detachment that has the Solar Auxilia faction and fulfils at least one of the following conditions may use
a Cohort Doctrine:

• The Detachment includes at least one model with the Cohort Doctrines special rule.

• The Detachment can upgrade at least one model from the Detachment to have the Cohort Doctrines
special rule as noted in a specific Cohort Doctrine that allows this

PAGE 83
COHORT DOCTRINE: SOLAR PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• The Support Section special rule in a detachment using this Cohort Doctrine changes the compulsory
choice in the rule to Veletaris Storm Sections rather than Auxilia Lasrifle Sections. Auxilia Lasrifle
Sections gain the Support Squad special rule.

• Veletaris Storm Sections in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select an Auxilia Arvus
Lighter Orbital Shuttle as a Dedicated Transport.



Limitations

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than one Heavy Support or Fast attack
choice combined with the Tank type (Super heavy tanks included)

• Sentry Gun Batteries and Auxilia Rapier Batteries all become 0-1 choices in a detachment using this
Cohort Doctrine.




                        COHORT DOCTRINE: ULTRAMAR PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine uses the Organisation chart shown below to select what units
are in an Auxilia Infantry Tercio instead of the one found in the Crusade Imperalis book. Veletaris Storm
Sections gain the Support Section Special rule.

• All Solar Auxilia Lasrifle Sections gain a bonus of +1 to all To Hit rolls made during Shooting Attacks
when all models in the unit are in base contact with at least one other model from the same unit.

Ultramar Pattern Auxilia Rifle Tercio Organisation Chart

An Ultramar Pattern Auxilia Infantry Tercio includes 1-6 sections (rather than 1-3)



Limitations

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not select Dedicated Transports for any Auxilia Infantry
Tercios, but may of course include an Aegis Defence line.

PAGE 84
COHORT DOCTRINE: REBORN COHORTS
Effects

• All models with the Infantry Type in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gain a bonus of +1 to
their Leadership Characteristic and the Stubborn special rule.

• When making a Shooting Attack during any Game Turn in which the attacking unit has not Moved, a
unit from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls of ‘1’ .



Limitations

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than one Heavy Support or Fast attack
choice combined with the Tank type (Super heavy tanks included)

• Sentry Gun Batteries and Auxilia Rapier Batteries all become 0-1 choices in a detachment using this
Cohort Doctrine.

• All models with the Infantry Unit Type in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine count their Initiative
as ‘1’ for the purposes of rolling as part of a Sweeping Advance, making any sort of Initiative test and
when determining which Initiative Step they would attack in during an Assault their Initiative
Characteristic is considered to be one lower than normal



                COHORT DOCTRINE: ARMOURED FIST PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Auxilia Leman Russ Strike Squadrons or Auxilia
Leman Russ Strike Squadrons as non-Compulsory Troops choices. An Auxilia Leman Russ unit selected
as a Troops choice in this manner may only consist of a single model,

• In a Primary Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine, a single Auxilia Tank Commander, must be
selected as a HQ choice. This Leman Russ Command Tank gains the Cohort Doctrines special rule and
must be selected as the army’s Warlord and must use the Armoured Legate Warlord trait (see below). A
model with the Vehicle Unit Type must be selected as the Warlord of an army using this Cohort
Doctrine, regardless of any rules which would require a model to be selected as the army’s Warlord
(note this means that some units and Characters cannot be selected as part of this army)

Warlord Trait: Armoured Legate - A Warlord with this Warlord Trait gains the Cohort Doctrines special
rule, a 5+ Invulnerable Save and increases its BS by +1.



Limitations

• All units composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type must begin the battle Embarked in a
Transport Unit or in be held in Reserves.

PAGE 85
COHORT DOCTRINE: PENAL PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• All models replace the Close Formation Fighting special rule from a Detachment using this Cohort
Doctrine with the Furious Charge special rule.

• Any model in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may replace a lasrifle or volkite charger with a
lascarbine, lasgun, stubcarbine, autorifle or shotgun for no additional points cost. In addition, one
Auxilia in any Solar Auxilia Lasrifle Section may replace a lasrifle with a heavy stubber for free.

• All models selected as part of a Solar Auxilia Lasrifle Section gain the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule –
this does not stack with any other variant of this special rule and if the unit has access to any other Feel
No Pain special rule, the controlling player must select one to use.



Limitations

• Auxilia Veletaris Sections in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gain the Support Section
Special rule.




                COHORT DOCTRINE: FERAL PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• Any unit made up entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type may be given the Fear special rule for a
cost of +25 points per unit.

• All units that include one or more models with the Close Formation Fighting special rule gain the
Counter-attack special rule while ‘In Formation ’ .



Limitations

• All units in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine that begin the controlling player’s Assault phase
with an enemy unit that is a valid target for a Charge must declare a Charge. If more than one enemy unit
is a valid target, the controlling player chooses which enemy unit is the target of the Charge.

• All other Detachments in an army with the Loyalist Allegiance that includes a Detachment using this
Cohort Doctrine will consider the Detachment with this Cohort Doctrine to be Distrusted Allies,
regardless of the normal result of the Allies Matrix

PAGE 86
COHORT DOCTRINE: SIEGE PATTERN COHORTS
Effects

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Auxilia Artillery Tank Batteries as both Elites and
Heavy Support choices.

• When a model from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine makes a Shooting Attack with any weapon
with the Barrage and/or Blast special rules, the controlling player may choose to re-roll the Scatter dice
(but not any D6 rolled to determine the distance of any scatter).



Limitations

• All units in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine with the option to select a Dedicated Transport
must select that option at the normal cost in points – but do not have to start the battle Embarked on that
Dedicated Transport.




                COHORT DOCTRINE: IRON PATTERN COHORT


Effects

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Castellax Maniples and Thallax Squads as Elites
choices.

• A Legate Marshal, Auxilia Marshal or Auxilia Captain in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may
select a cortex controller for +15 points each.

• Legate Commanders and Lord Marshals in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gains the Patris
Cybernetica special rule.



Limitations

• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than one Heavy Support or Fast attack
choice combined with the Tank type (Super heavy tanks included)

• Sentry Gun Batteries and Auxilia Rapier Batteries all become 0-1 choices in a detachment using this
Cohort Doctrine.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="ebc6a9e4-1fc6-519f-9d97-4390354d4c4f" name="New Warlord Traits — Sons of Horus" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="bb8dd1fa-3b09-555e-90e7-3e7588bd2050" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="b38119c6-829b-5645-9c90-6b498285e067" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 87-87" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 87
Legion Specific Warlord Trait Tables.
These are all completely optional and are mostly just ports of the 7th edition versions and the ones that don’t work were replaced with the
warlord traits from 2.0.




                                          SONS OF HORUS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE

     1. True Son: All models in the same detachment that can draw line of sight to the Warlord can use his
        leadership for making Morale, regroup or Pinning tests. In addition, the Warlord may reroll failed
        saving throws against wounds caused by Psychic Powers or Force Weapons.

     2. Eye of the Gods: At the beginning of every turn roll a D6, on a 1 the Warlord suffers a wound with no
        saves of any kind. On a 2-5 increase the Strength and toughness of the warlord by 1. On the roll of a 6
        The warlord regains a lost wound as well as the previous effect.



     3. The Armor of Pride: The first time in any battle when a Warlord with this Trait is reduced to 0 Wounds
        for any reason, the controlling player must immediately make a Leadership test for that model. If the
        Test is failed then the Warlord is removed as a casualty as normal, but if the Test is passed then the
        Warlord is not removed as a casualty, remains in play and regains D3 Wounds. This has no effect
        against attacks or rules which remove the model as a casualty without inflicting Wounds or against
        attacks with the Instant Death special rule.

     4. Unholy Fortitude: The Warlord has the It Will Not Die special rule.

     5. Soul Eater: If this model is attacking with a Melee weapon, it has the murderous strike special rule. If
        it already had the Murderous Strike special rule, any roll of a 5+ to wound gains the Instant Death
        special rule.

     6.   Cast in Gold: When the Warlord is engaged in a challenge with an enemy model that has a Weapon
          Skill that is equal to or greater than that of the Warlord’s, the Warlord gains +1 Strength and +1
          Attacks for the duration of the Challenge. Furthermore, if the Warlord removes an enemy model as a
          casualty during a challenge that had a weapon skill equal to or hire than the warlords.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="f6239ddc-ead6-57c0-ac55-7f3bf85349a8" name="New Warlord Traits — Iron Warriors and Word Bearers" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="9f2f25aa-4ad5-540b-a96c-3a9051e70206" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="5a4f35ff-3d09-533d-b644-65641dfa6fc3" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 88-88" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 88
IRON WARRORS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
1.   Iron Without: Your Warlord has the Feel No Pain (4+) special rule, which cannot be improved by any
     means.

2.   Cold Calculations: Your Warlord has the Fearless special rule.

3.   Master of Fortifications: After deployment, but before Scout redeployments and Infiltrate deployments,
     nominate one piece of terrain in your deployment zone (this cannot be one you have purchased as part of
     your army. The terrain piece's cover save is increased by 1 for the duration of the game (to a maximum of
     3+). Note that a piece of terrain can only be bolstered in this way once.

4.    Technoviral Manipulator: Once per game, in the shooting phase and instead of firing a weapon, The
     Warlord may make a Leadership test, if failed nothing happens, If Successful, the Warlord may select an
     enemy vehicle model within 12” inches. That vehicle immediately makes a shooting attack with one of its
     weapons as if it was the shooting phase.

5.    Steel Castellan:. Your Warlord and his unit have the Counter-attack and Split Fire special rules whilst in
     cover.

6.   Master of Blasphemous Machines:. Friendly vehicles in the same detachment have the It Will Not Die
     special rule whilst they are within 6" of your Warlord




                  WORD BEARERS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
1. Unholy Firebrand: Your Warlord has the Zealot special rule. If your Warlord already has the Zealot special
rule, then he and any models affected by his Zealot special rule can re-roll all failed To Hit rolls in every round of
close combat, not just the first.

2. Latent Powers: Your Warlord has the Psyker (Mastery Level 1) special rule, and can generate his powers from
the Daemonology (Malefic) discipline. If your Warlord is already a Psyker, add 1 to his Mastery Level instead.

3. The Voice of Lorgar: At the start of each of your turns, pick one of the following special rules to bestow upon a
single unit from a Word Bearers Detachment or Formation that is within 12" of your Warlord: Counter-attack,
Fearless, Furious Charge, Relentless. The unit you pick gains that special rule until the start of your next turn.

4. Unbreakable Devotion: Any units that include at least one model with the Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)
special rule and have at least one model within 6" of a Warlord with this Trait (including the Warlord himself and
any unit he has joined) automatically pass the first failed Morale check or Pinning test they are called upon to
make each turn.

5. Enslaved by Darkenss: Your Warlord increases his Strength and Toughness by 1 during turns 1 and 2. During
turns 3-4 his stats are normal but turns 5+ He decreases his Strength and Toughness by 1.

6. Iconoclast: A Warlord with this Trait, and any unit he has joined, gain a bonus of +1 Attack when locked in
combat with an enemy unit that includes at least one model with the Independent Character special rule, a
Legion vexilla or a Legion standard. When making a Shooting Attack or Melee Attack targeting a Fortification,
Building or other Terrain piece with a Toughness Characteristic, they gain a bonus of +2 to their Strength or the
Strength of any weapons used.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="d485930f-a464-50ae-b9f8-16ba436e753a" name="New Warlord Traits — Thousand Sons and Emperor’s Children" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="4f4aa1e8-c8bb-5df2-9224-9ce7042044e4" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="dce183ac-f958-5f3f-bbe7-474008b60e11" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 89-89" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 89
THOUSAND SONS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
1. Arrogance of Aeons: Your Warlord has the Adamantium Will special rule and can choose to re-roll
a single dice each time they make a Deny the Witch test.

2, Undying Form: Your Warlord has the Eternal Warrior special rule.

3. Aetherstride: Your Warlord and his unit are not slowed by difficult terrain and do not suffer the
penalty to their Initiative for charging through difficult terrain.

4. Lord of Forbidden Lore: Your Warlord knows one additional psychic power.

5. Walker of the Webway: Your Warlord and his unit have the Deep Strike special rule. If they already
had the Deep Strike special rule, then do not roll for scatter when they arrive by Deep Strike.

6. Lord of Flux: Enemy units within 12" of your Warlord treat all terrain, even open ground, as difficult
terrain. In addition, all models in any enemy units that Run, Turbo-boost, move Flat Out or charge
within 12" of your Warlord must take a Dangerous Terrain test




          EMPEROR’S CHIILDREN WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
1. Glutton for Punishment:. Your Warlord has the Eternal Warrior special rule.

2. Quicksilver Reflexes: Add 2 to your Warlord's Initiative characteristic.

3. Nexus of Debauchery: Add 1 to the Feel No Pain rolls of your Warlord and his unit, if they did not
already possess Feel no Pain, they gain Feel no Pain.

4. Psychotropic Aura:. Your Warlord has the Fear special rule. Any unit that is locked in combat with
your Warlord must take a Fear test with 3D6 instead of 2D6.

5. Stimulated by Pain: Your Warlord gains 1 Attack each time he loses a Wound. However, if he
recovers Wounds through any means, his Attacks are reduced accordingly.

6. Idol of Mindless Devotion:. Your Warlord can choose to automatically pass any Look Out, Sir rolls
he is required to make instead of rolling.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="2c963df3-8466-56cc-98a4-013a7f71b5b5" name="New Warlord Traits — Imperial Fists and Iron Hands" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="bad47d22-020f-5cf6-a5dd-46fff2d7a8a1" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="8b989f82-f22e-5591-ac92-fbd5ade8d840" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 90-90" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 90
IMPERIAL FISTS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
1. Solar Marshal: Your Warlord and all models in his unit gain +1 Weapon Skill when locked in combat with enemy units
with the Traitor allegiance.

2. Tenacious Opponent: Your Warlord has the It Will Not Die special rule.

3. Wise Commander: Whilst your Warlord is alive, you can choose to add or subtract 1 from any of your Reserve Rolls
(state which before the dice is rolled).

4. Indomitable: If your Warlord and his unit do not move in their Movement phase, then he and his unit have the Fearless
and Counter-attack special rules until the start of their next turn.

5. Architect of Devestation: This Warlord, and all models with the Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists) special rule in any
unit he joins, may re- roll failed T o Hit rolls of ‘1’ as long as that unit is entirely within an area of Terrain that grants a Cover
Save or Embarked within a Fortification

6. Fleet Commander:. Once per game, your Warlord can call down an orbital strike in his Shooting phase. This counts as
firing a ranged weapon with the profile below. This does not prevent the Warlord and his unit from declaring a charge
against the target unit that turn.

           Range               S         AP        TYPE

          Infinite             10        1         Ordnance 1, Barrage, Large Blast, Orbital



Orbital: If an arrow is rolled on the scatter dice, the blast marker scatters the full 2D6" - the Warlord's Ballistic Skill makes
no difference.

                                   IRON HANDS WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
     1. Adept of the Omnissiah: Your Warlord has the Blessing of the Omnissiah special rule. If the Warlord
        already has this special rule, he may re-roll any failed attempts to repair a vehicle.

     2. Will of Iron: Your Warlord has the Fearless special rule.

     3. All Flesh is Weakness: Your Warlord has +1 on any Feel No Pain rolls he makes. If he did not already
        get Feel no Pain somehow, He gains Feel No Pain 5+

     4. Student of History: Your Warlord and any Iron Hands unit he joins can choose to automatically fail
        any Morale check they are required to make.

     5. Merciless Resolve: Your Warlord and all friendly Iron Hands units within 12" of him have the
        Crusader special rule.

     6.   Target Protocols:. Your Warlord and any Iron Hands unit he joins re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 in the
          Shooting phase.

                               RAVEN GUARD WARLORD TRAITS TABLE</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="218b9d3c-917b-538b-9ffe-10ee47c29860" name="New Warlord Traits — Raven Guard and Ultramarines" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="3d929c95-9a2a-5dd5-8223-8eef2443ab66" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="09e81cfd-5394-5184-b6ee-cef3a48d91c8" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 91-91" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 91
1.   Vanish into the Gloom: When your Warlord's unit is chosen as the target of a shooting attack, it can
              immediately Vanish into the Gloom, moving up to D6". Models from your Warlord's unit that are in cover at
              the end of this move receive +1 to their cover saving throws against that shooting attack. The firing unit
              cannot choose a different target, even if your Warlord's unit is now out of range or line of sight. Your
              Warlord's unit can only Vanish into the Gloom once per turn and cannot do so at all if Falling Back or
              charging.

         2.   Concentrated Attack: At the start of your Charge phase, pick an enemy unit within your Warlord's line of
              sight. Until the end of the phase, Raven Guard units can re-roll charge rolls against that unit.

         3.   Master of Shadows: Once per game, as long as your Warlord is on the battlefield, you can declare in your
              Movement phase that Night Fighting rules are in effect until the start of your next turn.

         4.   Silent Stalker: Enemy units wishing to fire Overwatch at your Warlord or his unit must first pass a
              Leadership test. If your Warlord charged through difficult terrain, subtract 2 from the enemy unit's
              Leadership when they take this test.

         5.   Exit Strategy: When rolling for Variable Game Length, you can add or subtract 1 from the result if your
              Warlord is on the battlefield.

         6.   Swift and Deadly: Once per battle, your Warlord, and any unit he has joined, can charge even if they Ran in
              the preceding Shooting phase



                           ULTRAMARINES WARLORD TRAITS TABLE
    1.   Noble Visage: Your Warlord, and all friendly units within 12" of your Warlord with any Loyalist unit must re-roll
         failed Morale checks, Pinning tests and Fear tests.

    2.   Aegis of Wisdom: Any friendly unit made up entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
         special rule that can draw a line of sight to a Warlord with this Warlord Trait, may upon making a successful
         Regroup test, may make Shooting Attacks and declare Charges as normal, ignoring the normal restrictions for
         units that have Regrouped in the same turn.

    3.   Paragon of War. Your Warlord has the Preferred Enemy special rule.

    4.   Master of Strategy: You can add 4 to any roll to Seize the Initiative.

    5.   The Burden of Kings: In any Phase in which one or more Wounds has been allocated to a Warlord with this Trait,
         whether saved or unsaved, the Warlord gains the It Will Not Die (4+) and Fearless special rules until the end of
         the Warlord’ s controlling player’s next turn.
    6.   Adept of the Codex: Your Warlord and friendly units within 6" of him have the Split Fire special rule.




                             DARK MECHANICUM WARLORD TRAITS
Any Traitor faction Taghmata, Legio Cybernetica or Ordo Reductor army may roll on this table for Warlord Traits</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="6bcac874-c2f7-5e72-8e89-bbc9c62143c4" name="New Warlord Traits — Dark Mechanicum" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="58b1125e-2d7d-5563-9510-843f4e946481" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="87cd0661-b092-5c56-9c54-f02d9e542b6e" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="4f8912f9-c0d7-5973-a5df-d0b03f99f9c3" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 92-92" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 92
1.   Scion of Cyclothrathe

      An army that’s Warlord has this trait has the following effect. When rolling to determine the effect of a weapon
     with the Haywire special rule against a Daemon Engine, use the following Haywire Dampening table instead of
     the usual one.

     Haywire Dampening Table:

     When a weapon with the Haywire special rule Hits a model that is a Daemon engines, roll a D6 to determine the
     effect:

     D6 RESULT

     1-3 - No Effect.

     4-5 - Vehicles suffer a Glancing Hit.

     6- Vehicles suffer a Penetrating Hit.


2.   Scion of Xana II

     Once per game at the beginning of the movement phase, the Warlord may pick a friendly unit of models entirely
     composed of Daemon Engines. Improve the invulnerable save of the targeted unit by +1, to a maximum of 4+,
     until the beginning of the controlling player’s next turn.

3.   Scion of Retlaxi

     When a model that is a Daemon Engine that is part of the same Detachment as a Warlord with this Trait loses its
     last Hull Point, it always Explodes! And has the Pinning special rule.

4.   Scion of Sarum

     A single daemon engine unit in the same detachment as the warlord may be given the Implacable advance
     special rule.

5.   Scion of Incaladion

     Enemy models cannot fire overwatch within 6” of any Daemon engine.

6.   Scion of Uraniborg 1572

     The Warlord gains the implacable advance special rule.




                                                 New Rites of War
     Some legions will get a third Rite of War if they do not possess a Legiones Hereticus version of their rules. This is
     mainly because the Imperial Fists got a third Rite of War.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="a5507059-fe9e-5313-82ab-0b7b24639aff" name="Rite of War — Imperial Fists: Templar Assault" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="06512826-81fd-58cf-8330-dd0dd4d078bd" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="43be9f43-825c-5108-ac8e-ec911f1516ef" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 93-93" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 93
IMPERIAL FISTS RITE OF WAR
                               TEMPLAR ASSAULT

 “When the Templars of the Legion's Oaths go to war, they do so with duty and righteous purpose above all else,
 and cannot be halted except in death. The Templars strike with overwhelming force in crashing waves of power
             armour - their tactics are not subtle, but their methods are furious and irresistible. “


Sword Brethren:

Units of Templar Brethren may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War.

Heart of the Legion:

All models in a Templar Brethren unit taken as part of a Detachment using this Rite of and any
models attached to them gain Feel No Pain 6+ when controlling an objective. If they already
possessed Feel No Pain, it increases it by 1.

Black Judgment:

For the duration of any turn in which a unit of Templar Brethren taken as part of a Detachment using
this Rite of War Disembark from a vehicle, all models in the Disembarking unit gain the Rage special
rule (this does not apply if the unit is forced to make an Emergency Disembarkation).

Limitations

• A Detachment using this Rite of War must select Templar Brethren to fill all Compulsory Troops
choices in the Detachment.

• This Rite of War may only be taken for a Detachment in an army with the Loyalist Allegiance and all
Detachments..

• Detachments using this Rite of War cannot take more Elites and Fast Attack choices in total than
they have Troops choices in the Detachment. So, for example, a Detachment with three Troops
choices could take three choices made up of Fast Attack, Elites, or a combination of the two.




                           RAVEN GUARD RITE OF WAR
                  SHADOW WARDEN SHOCK ASSAULT</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="2f3ae317-669c-5db8-b8b1-9272bc4a8931" name="Rite of War — Raven Guard: Shadow Warden Shock Assault" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="eb0ee5c1-4562-5405-9ad7-31f30345672c" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="fffba35c-5cd7-54a7-8525-9ef4c86dbc9f" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 93-94" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 93
IMPERIAL FISTS RITE OF WAR
                               TEMPLAR ASSAULT

 “When the Templars of the Legion's Oaths go to war, they do so with duty and righteous purpose above all else,
 and cannot be halted except in death. The Templars strike with overwhelming force in crashing waves of power
             armour - their tactics are not subtle, but their methods are furious and irresistible. “


Sword Brethren:

Units of Templar Brethren may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War.

Heart of the Legion:

All models in a Templar Brethren unit taken as part of a Detachment using this Rite of and any
models attached to them gain Feel No Pain 6+ when controlling an objective. If they already
possessed Feel No Pain, it increases it by 1.

Black Judgment:

For the duration of any turn in which a unit of Templar Brethren taken as part of a Detachment using
this Rite of War Disembark from a vehicle, all models in the Disembarking unit gain the Rage special
rule (this does not apply if the unit is forced to make an Emergency Disembarkation).

Limitations

• A Detachment using this Rite of War must select Templar Brethren to fill all Compulsory Troops
choices in the Detachment.

• This Rite of War may only be taken for a Detachment in an army with the Loyalist Allegiance and all
Detachments..

• Detachments using this Rite of War cannot take more Elites and Fast Attack choices in total than
they have Troops choices in the Detachment. So, for example, a Detachment with three Troops
choices could take three choices made up of Fast Attack, Elites, or a combination of the two.




                           RAVEN GUARD RITE OF WAR
                  SHADOW WARDEN SHOCK ASSAULT

PAGE 94
“When the shadow falls, the dead do not rise.”

Thunderhawk Assault:

 If any jump pack units from this detachment are in Reserve or Ongoing Reserve, they will arrive at the same time
- if you need to make Reserve Rolls, make a single roll for all units from this this detachment with jump packs.
When they arrive from Reserve, draw a straight line from a point on any table edge to a point on the opposite
table edge. The first model in each unit attempting to deep strike must be placed on this line. Each unit must
attempt to Deep Strike onto a point on this line, and can re-roll the scatter dice when Deep Striking along this
line.

On Wings of Fire:

Once per game, in your Movement phase, you can declare that all models with the legions astartes Raven guard
special rule that are equipped with jump packs will disengage. Each unit that is on the battlefield is removed
from play, even if it is locked in close combat, and placed into Ongoing Reserve.

On Time...On Target:

Corax or your warlord with Legiones astartes Raven guard special rule and as long as every model in the unit is
equipped with a Jump Pack and they have made a successful deep strike using the Thunderhawk Assault special
rule as part of the Rite of War, they can make a disordered charge on the turn they arrive from Deep Strike.

Scout Support:

During the Shooting phase, each Recon marine Sergeant or Vigilator from this detachment can spot for another
unit with the Legiones astartes (Raven Guard) Special rule from this detachment within 9" instead of firing a
weapon. Weapons carried by the unit being spotted for gain the Ignores Cover special rule until the end of the
phase.

Restrictions

-Must take assault marines as compulsory troops choice, in addition a recon marine squad must also be taken
as another additional compulsory troops choice

-No fortifications or Allies, and this can only be taken as the primary detachment

-Can only take as many fast attack and heavy support units as you have troop choices EX - if you have 6 troops
choices you can take 3 fast attack and 3 heavy support

-No models in terminator armor may be taken




                            IRON HANDS RITE OF WAR
                            THE DEAD EARTH DOCTRINE</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="4bb0869d-04f1-51f9-866d-31db41761bce" name="Rite of War — Iron Hands: The Dead Earth Doctrine" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="441ea443-cc83-50c1-ba57-fbdc0ff7dc26" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="90a7e76d-6b99-5538-beb2-9ffc090dbda4" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 94-95" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 94
“When the shadow falls, the dead do not rise.”

Thunderhawk Assault:

 If any jump pack units from this detachment are in Reserve or Ongoing Reserve, they will arrive at the same time
- if you need to make Reserve Rolls, make a single roll for all units from this this detachment with jump packs.
When they arrive from Reserve, draw a straight line from a point on any table edge to a point on the opposite
table edge. The first model in each unit attempting to deep strike must be placed on this line. Each unit must
attempt to Deep Strike onto a point on this line, and can re-roll the scatter dice when Deep Striking along this
line.

On Wings of Fire:

Once per game, in your Movement phase, you can declare that all models with the legions astartes Raven guard
special rule that are equipped with jump packs will disengage. Each unit that is on the battlefield is removed
from play, even if it is locked in close combat, and placed into Ongoing Reserve.

On Time...On Target:

Corax or your warlord with Legiones astartes Raven guard special rule and as long as every model in the unit is
equipped with a Jump Pack and they have made a successful deep strike using the Thunderhawk Assault special
rule as part of the Rite of War, they can make a disordered charge on the turn they arrive from Deep Strike.

Scout Support:

During the Shooting phase, each Recon marine Sergeant or Vigilator from this detachment can spot for another
unit with the Legiones astartes (Raven Guard) Special rule from this detachment within 9" instead of firing a
weapon. Weapons carried by the unit being spotted for gain the Ignores Cover special rule until the end of the
phase.

Restrictions

-Must take assault marines as compulsory troops choice, in addition a recon marine squad must also be taken
as another additional compulsory troops choice

-No fortifications or Allies, and this can only be taken as the primary detachment

-Can only take as many fast attack and heavy support units as you have troop choices EX - if you have 6 troops
choices you can take 3 fast attack and 3 heavy support

-No models in terminator armor may be taken




                            IRON HANDS RITE OF WAR
                            THE DEAD EARTH DOCTRINE

PAGE 95
“We do not advance. We endure. And from our position, the earth dies.”



Comrades-in-Arms:

If an enemy unit declares a charge against a unit with the Legiones Astartes Iron Hands special rule, then any
unengaged Dreadnoughts and models with the Legiones Astartes Iron Hands special rule from this
detachment within 12" of the charging unit's target can choose to fire Overwatch as if they were also targets
of the charge (though they can still only fire Overwatch once per phase).

No Weakness, No Mercy:

All models in this formation that remained stationary in the movement phase and do not pile in during the
assault phase re-roll To Wound and Armour Penetration rolls of 1. This applies to both shooting and close
combat attacks.

Seize and Control:

All units in the formation within 12" of an Objective have the Stubborn special rule.




Restrictions:

-All troops choices must include the maximum number of models possible.

-No units with Deep Strike, Infiltrate, or Scout may be included.

-Only 1 Fast Attack choice allowed.

Warlord must be an Iron-Father and Must deploy on the battlefield (Inside a vehicle is fine)(not in Reserve)
and may not use a Bike, Jetbike, or Jump Pack.

Trust in Iron: May not take Allied Detachments or Fortifications.




                                  ULTRAMARINES RITE OF WAR</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="6af99904-7b2d-5b6f-8b38-2b7a05c3f71a" name="Rite of War — Ultramarines: The Victrix Phalanx" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="0cdc631a-9d42-57c0-a33d-edc437b3ca34" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="1c77e845-9097-584b-9801-013be4c69ffa" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 95-96" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 95
“We do not advance. We endure. And from our position, the earth dies.”



Comrades-in-Arms:

If an enemy unit declares a charge against a unit with the Legiones Astartes Iron Hands special rule, then any
unengaged Dreadnoughts and models with the Legiones Astartes Iron Hands special rule from this
detachment within 12" of the charging unit's target can choose to fire Overwatch as if they were also targets
of the charge (though they can still only fire Overwatch once per phase).

No Weakness, No Mercy:

All models in this formation that remained stationary in the movement phase and do not pile in during the
assault phase re-roll To Wound and Armour Penetration rolls of 1. This applies to both shooting and close
combat attacks.

Seize and Control:

All units in the formation within 12" of an Objective have the Stubborn special rule.




Restrictions:

-All troops choices must include the maximum number of models possible.

-No units with Deep Strike, Infiltrate, or Scout may be included.

-Only 1 Fast Attack choice allowed.

Warlord must be an Iron-Father and Must deploy on the battlefield (Inside a vehicle is fine)(not in Reserve)
and may not use a Bike, Jetbike, or Jump Pack.

Trust in Iron: May not take Allied Detachments or Fortifications.




                                  ULTRAMARINES RITE OF WAR

PAGE 96
THE VICTRIX PHALANX


“The phalanxes of Ultramar stand unbroken, their discipline turning the tide of battle where all else would falter.”

Testudo Troops:

Legion Breacher Siege Squads must be taken as the compulsory Troops choices. Legion Breacher Squads
and Invictus Suzaerin Squads that are entirely composed of models with the Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
Special rule ignore the negatives of Hardened armour such as ignoring the -1 to runs, charges and Sweeping
advances. In addition, all boarding shields in the army ignore the restriction that boarding shields do not grant
bonus attacks for having two close combat weapons.

Disciplined Advance:

Legion Breacher Siege Squads or Invictarus Suzerain Squads gain +1 Combat Resolution for each other unit
with the Legiones Astartes Ultramarines special rule within 6”.

Shock Deployment Doctrine

Legion Breacher Siege Squads and Invictarus Suzerain Squads may take an Anvillus Pattern Dreadclaw Drop
Pods or Legion Drop pods as a Dedicated Transport.

Legion Breacher Siege Squads numbering more than 10 models may instead take a Kharybdis Assault Claw
as a Dedicated Transport.

These Dedicated Transports do not use up a Force Organisation slot.



Limitations

• May not take more Fast Attack choices than Heavy Support choices.

• No Allied Detachments or Fortifications may be taken.

• In any mission where this is a factor, the player using a detachment that uses this rite of war must always be
the attacker.

• Post Calth: Remus Ventanus and Honored Telemechrus may not be included in a detachment using this
Rite of War</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="cbbe395b-9afc-503f-8cb7-f117a4e385c3" name="Rite of War — Iron Warriors: Grinding Judgement" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="a72ed3bd-75ed-5c08-97bc-4b5f570e1926" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="d087f808-ec0d-5a6c-a0fc-70f23dfcbd7e" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 97-97" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 97
IRON WARRIORS RITE OF WAR
                                        GRINDING JUDGEMENT
                             “Let the weak hide behind walls. We bring our own.”



Bastion Spearhead

All vehicles with a front armor of AV 14 within 6 inches of another vehicle with a front armor of AV 14 gain a 6+
invulnerable save

True Heart of Iron

When any legion Astartes Iron Warriors unit that disembarks from a front armor AV 14 vehicle, all attacks
(shooting and close combat) against that unit are at -1 str unit the end of your opponent’s next turn.

Hardened Gunlines

You may take Iron Havoc squads as Troops with the support squad special rule, but only if your army includes
at least two units with AV14 front armour per unit of Iron Havocs taken this way.



Restrictions

-The army must include at least three vehicles with AV14 front armour.

-No Jump Infantry, Bikes, or Jetbikes

-No Allied Detachments

-Traitor Only




                                THOUSAND SONS RITE OF WAR</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="2a1e6bb1-1989-536c-a7b9-e128cd7fd3c1" name="Rite of War — Thousand Sons: The Achaean Configuration" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="cf6b45ba-8258-5613-a397-52b3946e1a31" hidden="false" targetId="94323054-901d-5dcb-9611-10c363ce7bfa" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="3f354487-ce19-517f-8409-cdf5ae971bdc" name="HH3 Port Rules - pp. 98-98" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 98
THE ACHAEAN CONFIGURATION


Effects:

The Achaean Manifold - A detachment using this Rite of War may select Castellax-Achea Battle-Automata
maniples as non-compulsory Troops choices.

Anchors of the Prosperine Will - Castellax-Achea Battle-Automata maniples gain the Implacable Advance
special rule as long as that model is within 6” of a friendly model with both the Legiones Astartes (Thousand
Sons) and Psyker special rules.

Arcane Ablation Matrix: When selected for a detachment using this Rite of War, Castellax -Achaea Automata
do not use the Malign Unbinding Special rule, instead it is replaced with the following:

Any friendly model with the Psyker special rule that suffers Perils of the Warp while within 12” of one or more
Castellax-Achaea models may choose to allocate all Wounds caused by that Perils of the Warp result to a
single Castellax-Achaea model within range. Wounds allocated in this manner are resolved normally.




Restrictions:

Cortex-Bound Legions - Any Castellax-Achaea Automata units selected as Troops choices must include
more than one model. ⸻

The Covenant of Iron and Flesh - A Detachment using this Rite of War must include at least one Legion
Techmarine Covenant or Legion Numerologist Cabal and at least one Legion Praevian.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="0.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="054a6640-6fad-5f1b-b782-8267a8aa4bbf" name="Legion Master of Descent Consul" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="b5da029f-5e06-57a8-84c9-61f60bcaa647" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="ac29b795-d026-5f6d-9db9-d6e21bb639d5" name="HH3 Port Consul - p. 19" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 19
NEW CONSUL TYPES

Legion Master of Descent Consul                                                +65 points

Wargear and Special Rules

A Centurion with this consul type gains Artificer armor, a refractor field, jump pack and
Strato-Vox. Cannot be equipped with terminator armor, bike or jet bike. In addition, A
Master of Descent gains the Master of Descent special rule

Strato-Vox

Any reserve rolls for a unit that contains a model with a Strato-Vox are automatically
successful. In addition, while any models with equipped with a Strato-vox are on the
battlefield at the beginning of the turn; any reserves rolls for units that wish to deploy via
the deep strike special rule are considered automatically successful as long as they deploy
via the deep strike special rule.

Master of Descent

If a model with this special rule is in reserves and every model in the unit is either jump
infantry or jet pack infantry and wishes to deploy via deep strike, they may deep strike onto
the table on turn 1. Only one unit from an army may make use of this special rule per turn.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="65.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="b679e7e1-b5cd-5d70-b5ce-58306c76fe64" name="Legion Overseer Consul" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="407a3f73-c17d-55b8-9dd1-3c0472dbabe5" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="b127fff3-ec0e-599a-9ebb-4134ec2505d3" name="HH3 Port Consul - p. 20" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 20
Legion Overseer                                                                       +25 points

Wargear and Special Rules

A Centurion with this consul type gains the Overseer’s retinue, Master of Auxilia and
Support officer special rules.

A Legion Overseer may exchange their Chainsword for a Power lash or Power maul for 15
points

Power Lash

Range               Str       AP        Type

-                   -1        3         Melee, Shred, Reach
Reach

The model with this special rule fights at +1 Initiative

Overseer’s Retinue:

An army that includes a model with this special rule may take a Tercio of 1-3 Auxilia Lasrifle
Sections or 1-3 Imperialis Militia Infantry Squads with no Provenances, as part of the same Force
Organisation choice as the model with this special rule, as an Overseer’s Retinue. Note that any
unit selected through the use of this special rule may not take any Dedicated Transport or Aegis
defence line options. Any Solar Auxilia Rifles Sections included through the use of the Overseer’s
Retinue gain the Legiones Auxilia (X) special rule that corresponds with the Legiones Astartes (X)
special rule that the Legion Overseer they share a Force Organisation choice with has. Additionally,
all models in a Tercio selected as an Overseer’s Retinue use the Leadership Characteristic of the
model with the Legiones Overseer special rule.



Master of Auxilia:

 A model with this special rule must join a Auxilia LasRifle Section or Imperialis Militia Infantry
Squad, chosen by the controlling player that was selected as an Overseer’s Retinue during
deployment and once joined, may not voluntarily leave the unit during the course of any battle and
may only join units selected through the use of the Overseer’s Retinue special rule. Whilst part of a
unit selected as an Overseer’s Retinue, the Legion Overseer automatically passes Look out Sir!
rolls. Additionally, a model with the Master of Auxilia special rule is considered to have the same
variant of the Legiones Auxilia (X) special rule as the models in the unit that they have joined.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="25.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="2dcd2818-5f3e-518b-8ba4-dd2505fd4f96" name="Sons of Horus Legion Dark Emissary" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="84180c54-8477-5a23-add4-e441c439e0be" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="b010256a-7a0f-57ab-b439-ec4ab82a9113" name="HH3 Port Consul - p. 21" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 21
Legion Specific New Consul types

Sons of Horus Legion Dark Emissary                                               +25 points

Wargear

A Dark Emissary gains a Staff of Dark Authority at no additional points cost. A Dark
Emissary may not select a jump pack, Space marine Bike or Space Marine Jetbike.

Staff of Dark Authority

All models with the Traitor Allegiance within 6" of a model with a Staff of Dark Authority,
including that model, increases their Leadership to 10 when taking a Morale check or
Pinning test.


       S      AP      TYPE

       +1      3      Melee, Murderous Strike, Unwieldy




Special Rules

The Dark Emissary gains the Warmaster’s Eye special rule:

Warmaster’s Eye:

If a Dark Emissary is selected as a Compulsory HQ choice in an Allied Detachment that is
part of an army with the Traitor Allegiance, then all models in the Allied Detachment with
the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule gain the Stubborn special rule.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="25.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="933bad20-897f-5a48-ab4a-03ce1a67a1a3" name="Imperial Fists Legion Castellan" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="b2eb4b9e-6b7d-5d9b-97e8-1433217ade5c" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="d8d56c36-e930-506e-a398-0bc36260d85f" name="HH3 Port Consul - p. 22" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 22
Imperial Fists Legion Castellan                                                            +20 points

Wargear

A Legion Centurion with the Castellan upgrade gains Hardened armor at no additional cost.

A Legion Centurion with the Castellan upgrade must select one of the following options: -
Master-crafted heavy bolter ......................................................................................Free
- Master-crafted autocannon..............................................................................+5 points
- Iliastus assault cannon ...................................................................................+10 points

In addition, a Castellan may not select a jump pack, Legion Space marine bike, Legion
Space marine jetbike, combat shield, boarding shield, power fist, Solarite power gauntlet,
lightning claw(s) or any weapon with the Two-handed special rule.

Special Rules

A Castellan gains the Fire Support special rule.

Fire Support:

When making an attack with a Heavy weapon, a Castellan may increase the number of
attacks made with that weapon by +1 when making a Shooting Attack (for example, a
Castellan making a Shooting Attack with a Heavy 3 weapon would roll an additional dice for
its attacks, rolling four dice in total). In addition, any Legion Heavy Support Squads in the
same Detachment as a Castellan gain the Implacable Advance Special rule.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="6c002a92-d392-50fa-a9a5-dba13e017054" name="Emperor’s Children Legion Phoenix Warden" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="10558e9c-1ed5-57c4-bfcc-447b494893f2" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="a3c2df0f-c745-55b5-91c1-92f79ce7ec39" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="69422aa1-5991-5e0f-85b8-2587fd03a146" name="HH3 Port Consul - p. 23" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 23
Emperor’s Children Legion Phoenix Warden                                       +30 points

Wargear

A Legion Centurion with the Phoenix Warden upgrade gains a Phoenix Power Spear and an
Iron Halo at no additional cost.

In addition, a Phoenix Warden MUST be equipped with Tartaros Terminator Armor which is
not included in the cost.

Special Rules

A Legion Centurion with the Phoenix Warden upgrade and a Phoenix Terminator Squad that
he is attached to gain the Skill Unmatched Special rule. In Addition the Phoenix Warden has
the Living Icon Special rule.

Skill Unmatched

When a combat that involves one or models with this special rule is resolved, before the
start of Initiative step 10 the controlling player of any models in that combat with this
special rule may select one of the three following options and apply the effects of that
option to all models with this special rule for the duration of that Assault phase. When a
unit contains more than one model with this special rule, then all models in that unit must
select the same option if one is chosen:

• A Perfect Guard: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, any to hit rolls made by the opponent suffer a -1 to hit to a maximum of 6+, but must
reduce their Attacks Characteristic by -1.

• A Perfect Strike: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, they increase their to hit roll by +1 to a maximum of 3+, but must reduce their
Attacks Characteristic by -1.

• A Perfect Fury: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this
option, they must increase their Attacks by +1, but must reduce their Weapon Skill by -1.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="30.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="346787ac-e782-563c-9d4b-584a0500e3b9" name="Irradiation Blaster (replace Lightning cannon)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
            <ns0:condition field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="58b1125e-2d7d-5563-9510-843f4e946481" type="equalTo" />
          </ns0:conditions>
        </ns0:modifier>
      </ns0:modifiers>
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="7af4d3bb-8f5f-507d-9a3c-c40bc8606ee6" hidden="false" targetId="a10cd975-b606-5fb2-a525-30a822572658" primary="true" />
      </ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule id="a85ced1c-8e15-54f9-a596-af557fd3b96a" name="HH 1.41 Weapon Options" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>PAGE 7
Mechanicum Krios Irradiation engine
A Mechanicum Krios may exchange its Lightning cannon with an Irradiation Blaster for 40 points

Irradiation Blaster

An Irradiation Blaster has two profiles, one must be picked when firing and if part of a unit of Krios, they must all choose
the same one.

                                       Range              S         AP        TYPE

                      Focused          16’                7         3         Heavy 1, Fleshbane, Rad-Phage,

                                                                              Radiation Beam

                      Dispersed        Hellstorm          2         5         Heavy 1, Fleshbane, Rad-Phage,



Radiation Beam

When the weapon is fired, draw a 1" wide line from the end of the gun barrel up to the listed range of the weapon. The
initial target for the weapon (the first model in the beam ’ s path) must be an enemy model.

    -    All models (friend and enemy) caught in the beam area (excepting the ring tank) su er a hit with the listed pro le
         of the weapon, except Zooming Flyers, Swooping Monstrous Creatures, and Flying Gargantuan Creatures that
         cannot be affected or targeted.
    -    Units struck receive a number of hits equal to the number of their models caught in the path of the beam;
         casualties are removed from affected units using the normal rules for removing casualties.
    -    If the beam strikes a Super-heavy vehicle, Gargantuan Creature or large intact building/fortification (bastion
         sized or larger), the attack is blocked and its line of effect will go no further. The blocking target will, however,
         super 1+D3 separate hits, rather than just 1.
    -     If a vehicle transporting models suffers a penetrating hit from the Irradiation Blaster, the occupants inside suffer
         D6 Str 2 AP- Fleshbane hits, in addition to any other effects. Casualties are assigned by the controlling player.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      </ns0:rules>
      <ns0:costs>
        <ns0:cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="40.0" />
      </ns0:costs>
      <ns0:constraints>
        <ns0:constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="0ab6c879-3c47-5283-bd15-cf6099273a5d" type="max" />
      </ns0:constraints>
    </ns0:selectionEntry>
    <ns0:selectionEntry id="230088bf-95ca-5a50-9979-e45e35803c1f" name="Disintegrator Blaster (replace combi-bolter)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <ns0:modifiers>
        <ns0:modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
          <ns0:conditions>
